hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13201","13165 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim informed me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, who said: Salim said, he said: Ibn Umar said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"13202","13166 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which he used to swear was: No, by the Disposer of hearts."
"13203","13167 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that he used to revile al-Bayda or was about to revile it, and would say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not enter ihram except at Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"13204","13168 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated, Salim narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not enter ihram except from beside the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"13205","13169 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated, Zuhayr narrated (Ha). And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, both said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated, Salim informed me that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he met Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah, and that was before revelation had come down upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered him a tray in which there was meat, but he refused to eat, saying: I do not eat what they slaughter upon their sacrificial stones; I eat only that upon which the name of Allah has been mentioned."
"13206","13170 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, narrating from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Harithah al-Kalbi, the freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We used to call him only Zayd ibn Muhammad until the Qur'an came down: Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah."
"13207","13171 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from his father, that he narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he appointed Usamah ibn Zayd as commander and it reached him that people criticized Usamah ibn Zayd and impugned his command: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people and said: You criticize Usamah and impugn his command, though you did that with his father before; he was well worthy of command, and he was the most beloved of all people to me, and this one after him is the most beloved of people to me, so treat him kindly, for he is among your best. Salim said: I never heard Abd Allah narrate this hadith but he said: except Fatimah."
"13208","13172 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached while at al-Mu'arras in Dhu al-Hulayfah, in the belly of the valley, and said: You are in a blessed plain."
"13209","13173 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, concerning the dream of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Abu Bakr and Umar, who said: I saw people gathered; Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two, with weakness in his drawing, and Allah forgives him; then Umar ibn al-Khattab stood and it turned into a large bucket; I never saw a strong genius among people working as he worked, until people watered their camels to satiety."
"13210","13174 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated, from Salim, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garments out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of Allah, one side of my lower garment slackens unless I attend to it. He said: You are not of those who do it out of arrogance."
"13211","13175 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Amr ibn Aslam al-Himsi narrated, Salm ibn Maymun al-Khawwas narrated, from Ali ibn Ata, from Ubayd Allah al-Umari, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in a market among the markets: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, Allah writes for him a thousand good deeds."
"13212","13176 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated, Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Khashshab narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is below the ankles is in the Fire."
"13213","13177 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I saw in a dream that people were gathered; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah stood and drew a bucket or two, and in his drawing was weakness, and Allah forgives him; then Umar ibn al-Khattab took it and it turned into a large bucket; I never saw a strong genius working as he worked, until people watered their camels to satiety."
"13214","13178 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. Salim said: My father narrated to me that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, one side of my lower garment slackens unless I attend to it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You are not of those who do it out of arrogance."
"13215","13179 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: While Umar ibn al-Khattab was traveling in a caravan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard him swearing by his father, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers; whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or remain silent."
"13216","13180 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not enter Paradise, and three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection. As for those who will not enter Paradise: the one disobedient to his parents, the masculine woman who imitates men, and the dayyuth. And as for the three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of what he gave."
"13217","13181 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: You know that in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to say: Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman, meaning regarding the caliphate."
"13218","13182 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamdani narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar informed me, from Nafi' and Salim, that Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and Isha after the twilight had disappeared by an hour."
"13219","13183 - Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Ash'ath narrated, Abu Asim narrated, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Ashura and said: It was the fast of the people of ignorance; whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break fast."
"13220","13184 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, make witr with one."
"13221","13185 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Raja al-Sakhtiyani narrated, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a source, and the source of piety is the hearts of the knowers."
"13222","13186 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me that Salim narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living."
"13223","13187 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jallalah, its milk, and riding it."
"13224","13188 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated, in the year 181, Umar ibn Hamzah al-Umari informed me, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you can be like the owner of the farq of rice, let him be like him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the owner of the farq of rice? He said: Three men went out, the sky clouded over them, so they entered a cave; a rock came until it sealed the door upon them, and they tried to move it but could not. One of them said to the others: You have fallen into a grave matter, so let each man supplicate with the best deed he did; perhaps Allah will save us from this. Then he mentioned the hadith of the cave in full."
"13225","13189 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated, Abu Aqil narrated, from Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his uncle Salim, and Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not the right of a Muslim man to spend a night of time except with his will present with him, when he has wealth about which a will is made."
"13226","13190 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib and al-Hasan ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, both said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, then Abu Bakr, then Umar; then the people of al-Baqi' will come and be gathered with me, then I will wait for the people of Makkah and they will be gathered with me."
"13227","13191 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated, Khalid ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the chest of Umar ibn al-Khattab with his hand when he became Muslim three times, saying: O Allah, remove what is in his chest of rancor and replace it with faith, saying that three times."
"13228","13192 - Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, my grandfather Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbir, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When his seventh day comes, shed blood on his behalf and remove harm from him."
"13229","13193 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah informed me, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a livestock dog or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day."
"13230","13194 - Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Adam narrated (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to lighten, yet he would lead us with al-Saffat."
"13231","13195 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at the old adulterer, nor the poor arrogant one, nor the one who drags his lower garment out of arrogance."
"13232","13196 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Salim, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Hajj and Umrah, whenever he came upon a pass or a highland he would say takbir three times, then say: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, praising our Lord; Allah fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone."
"13233","13197 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will descend at this salty plain; the last to go out to him will be women, until a man will return to his mother, his sister, and his paternal aunt and bind them with ropes fearing they will go out to him; then Allah will give the Muslims power over him and they will kill him and kill his followers, until the Jew will hide beneath a tree or a stone, and the stone or tree will say: O Muslim, this is a Jew beneath me, so kill him."
"13234","13198 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from Qahtan will surely drive people with a stick."
"13235","13199 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant makes an image but it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you created."
"13236","13200 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Sadusi, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, they said: Asim ibn Ali narrated, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah loves the skilled worker."
"13237","13201 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat saying: To You hastens the troubled she-camel, its saddle contradicting the religion of the Christians is its religion. Abu al-Qasim said: In my view Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman erred in raising this hadith to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because what is well known in narration from Ibn Umar is from Arafat while saying, then he mentioned the rajaz."
"13238","13202 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No servant makes an image but it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you created."
"13239","13203 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated, my grandfather narrated to me (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated, from Hanzalah, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House."
"13240","13204 - Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Halabi narrated, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds."
"13241","13205 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the tail-less one, for they seek sight and cause pregnancy to miscarry; whoever does not kill them is not of us."
"13242","13206 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated, from his father, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds, and a qirat is like Uhud."
"13243","13207 - Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Musa al-Wasiti narrated, my father narrated, Ghiyath ibn Ibrahim narrated, from Ash'ab the greedy ibn Abi Humaydah, who said: I came to Salim ibn Abd Allah asking him, and he looked down upon me from a small door, saying: Woe to you, O Ash'ab, do not ask, for my father narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People will surely come on the Day of Resurrection with not a shred of flesh on their faces, having worn it out."
"13244","13208 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Rawh ibn Salah narrated, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray before the sermon on the two Eids."
"13245","13209 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated, both said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Letting down the lower garment, the shirt, and the turban are alike; whoever drags any of them out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13246","13210 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated, Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated, from al-A'mash, who said: Salim ibn Abd Allah was sitting with al-Hajjaj, and al-Hajjaj said to him: Stand and strike the neck of this man. So Salim took the sword and took the man and headed toward the palace gate; his father looked at him as he headed off with the man and said: Do you think he will do it? He sent him back twice or thrice, and when he went out with him Salim said to him: Did you pray the morning prayer? He said: Yes. He said: Then take whichever road you wish. Then he came and threw down the sword, and al-Hajjaj said to him: Did you strike his neck? He said: No. He said: Why? He said: I heard this father of mine say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah until evening. Ibn Umar said: You are prudent; we named you Salim that you may be safe."
"13247","13211 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id narrated, my father narrated that al-Hajjaj ordered Salim ibn Abd Allah to kill a man. Salim said to him: Did you pray Fajr? The man said to him: Yes. He said: Go on. Al-Hajjaj said to him: What prevented you from killing him? Salim said: My father narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays Fajr is under Allah's protection for his day. I disliked killing a man whom Allah had granted protection. Al-Hajjaj said to Ibn Umar: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Ibn Umar said: Yes."
"13248","13212 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari, that he heard Salim ibn Abd Allah saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"13249","13213 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated, al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated, Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Dhimari narrated to me, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"13250","13214 - Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Isa ibn Hilal al-Himsi narrated, Abu Haywah Shurayh ibn Yazid narrated, from Khulayd ibn Da'laj, from Asim ibn Razin, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father: that he used to dye his beard yellow, wear sandals without hair, touch the two corners: the Black Stone and the Yemeni corner, and leave the two corners in the Hijr. And Ibn Umar narrated that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing that."
"13251","13215 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated, Salim ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: How is the night prayer? He said: Two by two; when you fear dawn, make witr with one."
"13252","13216 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated, Abd Allah ibn al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and became confused in it; when he finished, he said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Did you pray with us? He said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from prompting me?"
"13253","13217 - Abu Zakariyya al-Dinawari al-Basri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Husri narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrating from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None touches the Qur'an except one who is pure."
"13254","13218 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-San'ani narrated, from Hud ibn Ata, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought nabidh and drank from it."
"13255","13219 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated, Ali ibn Hawshab narrated, from Abu Qabil, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take mosques as pathways except for remembrance or prayer."
"13256","13220 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, Salim ibn Abd Allah informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount rose with him."
"13257","13221 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, from Salim, from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah had ten wives under him in ignorance; he became Muslim and they became Muslim, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Choose four of them."
"13258","13222 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Nu'man ibn al-Mundhir, who said: Salim ibn Abd Allah claimed, from his father, and Urwah claimed, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the days during Hajj and cannot find a sacrificial animal, when he performs tamattu', it is from the ihram of one of you until the Day of Arafah; that is the last of them."
"13259","13223 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated, Qatadah ibn al-Fudayl al-Ruhawi narrated, saying: I heard Abu Hadir narrating from al-Wadin ibn Ata al-Dimashqi, from Salim, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The poor of my Ummah will enter Paradise forty autumns before their rich. I said: Describe them to us. He said: They are those whose garments are soiled, whose heads are disheveled, who are not permitted at gates, who do not marry inaccessible women; the easts and wests of the earth are entrusted to them; they give all that is upon them, and are not given all that is theirs."
"13260","13224 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Ruhawi narrated, Qatadah ibn al-Fudayl narrated, from Abu Hadir, from al-Wadin, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Jews were asked about Musa and they spoke excessively, adding and omitting until they disbelieved; the Christians were asked about Isa and they spoke excessively about him, adding and omitting until they disbelieved; and narrations from me will surely spread, so whatever hadith of mine comes to you, recite the Book of Allah and weigh it thereby: what agrees with the Book of Allah, I said it; what does not agree with the Book of Allah, I did not say it."
"13261","13225 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated (Ha). And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, both said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from Shabib ibn Abd al-Malik, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah forbade wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"13262","13226 - Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Mada'ini, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated, Ali ibn Thabit narrated, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi' al-Uqayli, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, regarding His saying: Like a niche, he said: The interior of Muhammad, the glass is his heart, the lamp is the light in his heart. Kindled from a blessed tree: the tree is Ibrahim. An olive, neither eastern nor western: neither Jewish nor Christian. Then he recited: Ibrahim was neither a Jew nor a Christian, but a hanif, a Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists."
"13263","13227 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi narrated, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, and a man was turning pebbles with his hand. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he turned to us and said: Which of you was turning pebbles with his hand? A man stood and said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said to him: That is your share of your prayer."
"13264","13228 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated, Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in the congregation of women nor at a dead person, for when they gather they say this and that."
"13265","13229 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated (Ha). And Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Rasibi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi narrated, both said: Abu Asim narrated, from Abu Ubaydah of the descendants of Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus until it consumes him is better for him than that it be filled with poetry. And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna gave the lineage of Abu Ubaydah, saying: Abu Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"13266","13230 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated, Abu Matar narrated to me that he heard Salim ibn Abd Allah narrating from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard thunder and thunderbolts, he would say: O Allah, do not kill us with Your anger, do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us health before that."
"13267","13231 - Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Malik al-Awsabi al-Himsi narrated, Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated, al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ayyub, meaning al-Sakhtiyani, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he would raise his hands when beginning, when saying takbir for bowing, and when raising his head from bowing."
"13268","13232 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Attar narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated, from a man called al-Qasim, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, the Muslims looked to the best of them and appointed him successor, and he was Abu Bakr; when Abu Bakr died, he looked to the best of the Muslims and appointed him successor, and he was Umar; when he died or was killed, the Muslims looked to the best of them and appointed him successor, and he was Uthman. If you kill him, bring me one better than him; by Allah, I do not think you will do so. Abu al-Qasim said: Al-Qasim from whom Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated this hadith is Abu Nuhayk, a Basran, son of Muhammad."
"13269","13233 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, Kathir ibn Qunbur narrated, saying: We asked Salim ibn Abd Allah about the prayer of his father while traveling, and he informed me from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a matter comes upon one of you and he fears missing it, let him pray this prayer, meaning combining the two prayers."
"13270","13234 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Hafs al-Ansari narrated, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Sa'di narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No father grants his child anything better than good manners."
"13271","13235 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, both said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated, Yazid ibn Aban narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I forbade you from the nabidh of jars, and I had forbidden you from visiting graves, and I had forbidden you regarding sacrificial meats. Know that vessels neither permit anything nor forbid it; visit graves, for they soften hearts. Abdan added in his hadith: Know that I forbade you from the meats of sacrifices, so eat and store as you wish."
"13272","13236 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight, so gather over it and do not separate from it."
"13273","13237 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Muhammad al-Sami narrated, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated, Amr ibn Dinar, steward of the family of al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about a man, saying: Who knows him? A man among them said: I. He said: His name? He said: I do not know. He said: His father's name? He said: I do not know. He said: His dwelling? He said: I do not know. He said: This is not knowledge, until you know his name, his father's name, and his tribe; if he falls ill you visit him, and if he dies you follow his funeral."
"13274","13238 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated, saying: I heard Salim saying: Ibn Umar narrated to me that he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of his companions, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O you, do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not know that Allah revealed in His Book: whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah? They said: Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and that obeying Allah includes obeying you. He said: Obeying Allah is that you obey me, and obeying me includes that you obey your leaders; even if they pray sitting, pray sitting all together."
"13275","13239 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, both said: Abu Sadaqah Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-Qaratisi narrated, Ubayd ibn Ziyad al-Hadrami narrated to me, saying: Malik ibn Dinar met Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was riding a donkey with drooping ears, with worn saddle and clothes, and Salim said to him: From where is the man? He said: From you and to you and from some of your freedmen. He said: Narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him, does not betray him, and does not abandon him in a calamity that befalls him; though the best of Arabs and freedmen perish, loving one another with a love from which they find no escape, and though the worst of the two groups perish, hating one another with a hatred from which they find no escape."
"13276","13240 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are but like a hundred camels; riding camels are sought among people and hardly one is found."
"13277","13241 - Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated, Abd al-Razzaq narrated, my father narrated, from Harun ibn Qays, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on my brother Abd Allah ibn Rawahah; wherever prayer overtook him, he would make his camel kneel."
"13278","13242 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated, al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a day of Eid and began by praying without adhan or iqamah, then delivered the sermon."
"13279","13243 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jandal ibn Waliq narrated, Hushaym narrated, al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he began prayer he would raise his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and would not lift them beyond his ears."
"13280","13244 - Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from his father: al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon the camel wherever it turned with him."
"13281","13245 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave charity of a horse in the path of Allah to a man, then Umar found him selling it; he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave charity of a horse to so-and-so, and I found him selling it; shall I buy it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity."
"13282","13246 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated, saying: I found in the book of my maternal uncle, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, who informed him, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The keys of the unseen are five. Then he recited this verse: Allah has knowledge of the Hour, sends down rain, knows what is in wombs; no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; Allah is Knowing, Aware."
"13283","13247 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu al-Zinad, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: that some people raided the camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drove them off, apostatized from Islam, and killed the believing shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them; they were caught, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes. It is said: This is Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, and it is said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, and Allah knows best."
"13284","13248 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to me, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) branded the eyes of the Uranis only because they had branded the eyes of the shepherds."
"13285","13249 - Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father: al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated (Ha). And Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Adam narrated (Ha). And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, from Utbah ibn Muslim, from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Omen is in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse."
"13286","13250 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: I had a wife whom I loved, and my father disliked her, so he ordered me to divorce her, but I refused. Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abd Allah, divorce her."
"13287","13251 - Bilal ibn Abd Allah, from his father: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated, Urabi ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah al-Saba'i, Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me that his father Abd Allah ibn Umar said one day: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women their shares of mosques. I said: As for me, I shall prevent my family; whoever wishes may let his family go. He turned to me and said: May Allah curse you, may Allah curse you, may Allah curse you; you hear me say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they not be prevented, yet you say this. Then he wept and stood up angry."
"13288","13252 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, Ka'b ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Bilal ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women their shares of mosques when they seek your permission. Bilal said: By Allah, we shall surely prevent them. Abd Allah said: O enemy of Allah, I say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, yet you say: we shall prevent them."
"13289","13253 - Aban ibn Uthman, from Ibn Umar: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Abu Ma'shar narrated, Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Aban ibn Uthman narrated to me, my father Umar ibn Aban narrated, from his father, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with Aishah behind him, Abu Bakr sought permission and entered, then Umar sought permission and entered, then Sa'd ibn Malik entered, then Uthman ibn Affan sought permission while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was conversing with his knee uncovered; he extended his garment over his knee when Uthman sought permission, and said to his wife: Move back. They conversed a while then left. Aishah said: O Prophet of Allah, my father and his companions entered, yet you did not adjust your garment from your knee, nor move me away from you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, shall I not be shy of a man of whom the angels are shy? By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of the Messenger of Allah, the angels are shy of Uthman as they are shy of Allah and His Messenger; had he entered while you were near me, he would not have spoken nor raised his head until he left."
"13290","13254 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Abu Ma'shar narrated, Ibrahim ibn Umar narrated, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): was in a garden; Abu Bakr sought permission, and he said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Then Umar sought permission, and he said: Permit him, give him glad tidings of Paradise and of martyrdom. Then Uthman sought permission, and he said: Permit him, give him glad tidings of Paradise and of martyrdom."
"13291","13255 - Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated, Abu Ja'far, meaning Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali, narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent your women from coming to mosques."
"13292","13256 - Musa ibn Talhah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Talhah ibn Yahya, my uncle Musa ibn Talhah narrated to me, saying: I traveled with Ibn Umar between Makkah and Madinah, and he would not exceed two rak'ahs, praying neither before them nor after them, saying: I pray as I saw my companions pray, and I do not prevent anyone who wishes to add good."
"13293","13257 - Isa ibn Talhah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from his uncle Isa ibn Talhah, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar in travel, and he would not exceed two rak'ahs, while his sons and companions would perform voluntary prayers. I said: Why do you not perform voluntary prayer? He said: I do only as I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"13294","13258 - Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the edge of the sun inclines, delay prayer until it emerges; when the edge of the sun disappears, delay prayer until it has set."
"13295","13259 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not seek to pray at sunrise or sunset, for it rises with the two horns of Satan."
"13296","13260 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated, Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman for part of his rule."
"13297","13261 - Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No household is given gentleness but it benefits them."
"13298","13262 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of his family."
"13299","13263 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the well of Badr, then he mentioned the hadith."
"13300","13264 - Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, al-Awza'i narrated, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we enter upon rulers; one of them judges unjustly, and we say: May Allah grant you success, and he looks at one of us and praises him. He said: As for we, the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to count it hypocrisy; what do you count it as?"
"13301","13265 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun al-Qazzaz al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: I came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we sit with rulers; they speak words while we know the truth is otherwise, yet we affirm them; they judge unjustly and we support them in it and commend it to them. What do you think of that? He said: O son of my brother, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to count this hypocrisy."
"13302","13266 - Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar: Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, who said: Ibn Umar entered upon Abd Allah ibn Amir visiting him ill, and he said: O Ibn Umar, will you not supplicate for me? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from plunder. And you were over Basrah."
"13303","13267 - Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Umar: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ali ibn Sa'id al-Raqqi narrated, Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from al-Zuhri, from Salim and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed the fear prayer with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he lined up a group of us behind him, and a group faced the enemy; he said takbir then bowed with them and prostrated two prostrations, then the group with him turned and faced the enemy, and the other group came and lined up behind him; then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam, and each man of the two groups stood and made up for himself one rak'ah and two prostrations."
"13304","13268 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Hammam narrated, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Ibn Umar narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"13305","13269 - Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him thereby."
"13306","13270 - Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: I came to Ibn Umar while he was sitting on the pavement with people praying, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do you not pray? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not pray a prayer twice in one day."
"13307","13271 - Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik (Ha). And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Malik narrated to me (Ha). And Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated, Malik informed me, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, that he said: I was traveling with Ibn Umar on the road to Makkah. Sa'id said: When I feared dawn, I dismounted and performed witr. Abd Allah said: Is there not in the Messenger of Allah a good example for you? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr upon the camel."
"13308","13272 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying voluntarily upon his donkey while proceeding to Khaybar."
"13309","13273 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated, from Malik (Ha). And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to me, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated, Malik narrated to me, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon his donkey while facing Khaybar."
"13310","13274 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from Amr ibn Yahya, Sa'id ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while upon a donkey facing Khaybar. Amr ibn Yahya said: And it is toward Syria."
"13311","13275 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Amr ibn Yahya informed me, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon his donkey, with his donkey facing Khaybar, gesturing with gestures."
"13312","13276 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, Sa'id ibn Yasar, freedman of Shuqran, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey facing Khaybar."
"13313","13277 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated, Mindal narrated, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while facing Khaybar."
"13314","13278 - Muslim ibn Jundub, from Ibn Umar: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated, Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Jundub narrated, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever dies separating from the community dies a death of ignorance."
"13315","13279 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated (Ha). And Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated, both said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated, Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Jundub narrated to me, from his father, that he entered with Abd Allah ibn Umar upon Ibn Muti', saying: Peace be upon you. He said: Upon you peace and Allah's mercy; welcome to Abu Abd al-Rahman; place a cushion for him. Ibn Umar said: Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Three are not refused: milk, a cushion, and perfume, I would not have sat upon it."
"13316","13280 - Muslim al-Khayyat, from Ibn Umar: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Muslim al-Khayyat, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade intercepting incoming caravans, forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin, and forbade any of you proposing over his brother's proposal until he marries or leaves off."
"13317","13281 - Hakim ibn Abi Hurrah al-Aslami, from Ibn Umar: Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated, from Musa ibn Uqbah, Hakim ibn Abi Hurrah al-Aslami narrated to me that he heard a man asking Abd Allah ibn Umar about a man who vowed that no named day would come upon him but he would be fasting it, and it coincided with the Day of Sacrifice or the Day of Fitr. Ibn Umar said: There was for you in the Messenger of Allah a good example; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast the Day of Sacrifice nor the Day of Fitr, nor command fasting them."
"13318","13282 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated, Junadah ibn Salm narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Hakim, who said: I heard a man seeking a ruling from Ibn Umar about a man who vowed a vow on a day among days that that day would not pass him but he would be fasting; that day coincided with the Day of Sacrifice or the Day of Fitr. Ibn Umar said to him: There was for you in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a good example. Then he said: He would not fast the Day of Fitr nor the Day of Sacrifice, nor consider fasting it right."
"13319","13283 - Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Umar: Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated, Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Mounts are saddled only to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of Madinah, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis."
"13320","13284 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, who informed him, and Wahb had met Abd Allah ibn Umar: that Ibn Umar saw a shepherd and sheep in an unsightly place, while Ibn Umar had seen a better place than it. Ibn Umar said: Woe to you, O shepherd, move them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every shepherd is responsible for his flock."
"13321","13285 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Ma'n ibn Isa narrated, Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your span among the past nations is but as between the Asr prayer and sunset."
"13322","13286 - Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Umar: Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every entrusted one is asked about what he was entrusted with, until a man is asked about his wife, his servant, and his child."
"13323","13287 - Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Ibn Umar: Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Suraqah, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until blight passes. Ibn Suraqah said: When is that, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: The rising of the Pleiades."
"13324","13288 - Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Umar: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, that Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah said: A man prayed beside Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and heard him when he gave salam saying: You are Peace, and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor. Then he prayed beside Abd Allah ibn Umar and heard him when he gave salam saying the like of that, so the man laughed. Ibn Umar said to him: What made you laugh? He said: I prayed beside Abd Allah ibn Amr and heard him saying the like of what you said. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say that."
"13325","13289 - Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ibn Umar: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Malaki narrated, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the lost item, that he used to say: O Allah, Returner of the lost, Guide of the stray, guiding from straying, return to me my lost item by Your power and authority, for it is of Your giving and bounty."
"13326","13290 - Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar: Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah and Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iblis entered Iraq and fulfilled his need therein, then entered Syria and they drove him out, then entered Egypt and laid eggs therein and hatched, and spread his carpet."
"13327","13291 - Abu Alqamah, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Ibn Umar: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub al-Makhzumi, from Abu Alqamah, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were praying after Fajr and said: There is no prayer after Fajr except two rak'ahs."
"13328","13292 - Nu'aym al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is to mid-calves; there is no sin upon him in what is between that and the ankles; whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him."
"13329","13293 - Muhammad ibn Abi Hakim, from Ibn Umar: Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, from Abu al-Aswad, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hakim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is but the likeness of a tree whose leaves do not fall: the date palm."
"13330","13294 - Nu'aym al-Mujmir and Salim, from Ibn Umar: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubayd Allah, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir and Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever strikes his servant a prescribed punishment he did not deserve, its expiation is freeing him."
"13331","13295 - Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn Umar: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated, Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im narrated to me, claiming that he was sitting with Ibn Umar when a young man passed by him wearing a San'ani cloak dragging it loosely. He said: O young man, come here. The young man said to him: What do you need, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: Woe to you, do you love that Allah look at you on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Glory be to Allah, what prevents me from loving that? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah will not look at a servant on the Day of Resurrection who drags his lower garment out of arrogance. He said: That young man was seen only with garment tucked up until he died."
"13332","13296 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Ubadah ibn Muslim narrated, Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr narrated that he was sitting with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his supplication in the morning and evening, which he never left until he parted the world, until he died: O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my world, my family, and my wealth; O Allah, cover my faults and secure my fears; O Allah, guard me from before me, from behind me, from my right, from my left, from above me, and I seek refuge in You from being seized from beneath me. Jubayr said: And it is sinking. I do not know whether it is the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or the saying of Jubayr."
"13333","13297 - Qudamah ibn Ibrahim al-Juhami, from Ibn Umar: Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim narrated to us (Ha). And Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated, Sadaqah ibn Bashir, freedman of the Umariyyin, narrated, saying: I heard Qudamah ibn Ibrahim al-Juhami narrating that he used to frequent Abd Allah ibn Umar, saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to them: that a servant among Allah's servants said: O Lord, praise be to You as befits Your majestic face and Your mighty sovereignty. It confounded the two angels, and they did not know how to write it, so they ascended to heaven and said: O our Lord, Your servant said a saying we do not know how to write. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said, while He knows best what His servant said: What did My servant say? They said: O Lord, he said: O Lord, praise be to You as befits Your majestic face and Your mighty sovereignty. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said to them: Write it as My servant said, until My servant meets Me and I reward him for it."
"13334","13298 - Sa'id, from Ibn Umar: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated, Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for livestock except what is beyond the enclosure, nor for fruit except what the threshing floor shelters."
"13335","13299 - Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the weeping of the living."
"13336","13300 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman al-Nahartiri narrated, Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting for three days. They said: You fast continuously. He said: I remain with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"13337","13301 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: With the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions numerous, we used to count: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, then fall silent."
"13338","13302 - Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun, from Ibn Umar: Mu’adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated, from his father, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: We went in the morning with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Arafah; some of us said talbiyah and some said takbir; the one saying takbir was not blamed for his takbir, nor the one saying talbiyah for his talbiyah. And Abd Allah ibn Umar was among those who said takbir."
"13339","13303 - Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Umar: Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, saying: I heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sari which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, mentioned: Your Lord has placed beneath you a sari, is a river Allah brought forth for her to drink from."
"13340","13304 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated, Abu Awanah narrated, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and Ibn Umar, and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it, nor drinks wine while he is a believer when he drinks it, nor steals while he is a believer when he steals it, nor plunders a plunder of eminence while he is a believer."
"13341","13305 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Nadr Abu Umar narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Order him to take her back."
"13342","13306 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, I think from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise."
"13343","13307 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Qatan ibn Wahb, that Yuhannas, the freed slave of al-Zubayr, informed him that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar during the tribulation, and a freed slave woman of his came greeting him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I intended to go out, and the times have become hard upon us. Abdullah ibn Umar said to her: Sit, you foolish woman, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13344","13308 - Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qays al-Madani Abu Hazim say: Ibn Umar says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, then gives charity on Friday from his wealth, however little, will be forgiven every sin he committed until he becomes like the day his mother bore him, free of sins."
"13345","13309 - Abu Shuayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qays al-Madani say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An angel from heaven descended upon me who never descended upon any prophet before me, nor will descend upon anyone after me, and he is Israfil, and with him is Jibril. He said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. Then he said: I am a messenger of your Lord to you; He commanded me to give you the choice: if you wish, a Prophet-servant, and if you wish, a Prophet-king. I looked at Jibril, and Jibril signaled to me to be humble. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that: A Prophet-servant. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I said, a Prophet-king, then had I wished, the mountains would have moved with me as gold."
"13346","13310 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qays say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this young goat is to its owners. Had the world been equal in the sight of Allah to the weight of a mustard seed, He would not have given it except to His allies and His beloved ones among His creation."
"13347","13311 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qays say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is the Living Who does not die, in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Powerful, seeking thereby only His Face, Allah will admit him thereby into the Gardens of Bliss."
"13348","13312 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abdullah ibn Umar, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed me, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Ibn Umar, he said: I climbed above a roof and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Hafsah, relieving himself between two bricks, facing toward Bayt al-Maqdis."
"13349","13313 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, that he asked Ibn Umar about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When he prayed, he said Allahu Akbar every time he raised and every time he lowered in bowing and prostration, and when he finished he said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, to his right and to his left."
"13350","13314 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abdullah ibn Umar, and Malik ibn Anas, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I saw you wearing these leather sandals without hair. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing them and performing ablution in them."
"13351","13315 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Makki narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Said al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ibn Umar, and he mentioned the hadith."
"13352","13316 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Hakim al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Said al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it concerning the two leather sandals and the Corner."
"13353","13317 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, that he saw Ibn Umar dyeing with yellow and informing that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dye with it."
"13354","13318 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarkhi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Isa son of Maryam wearing a striped outer garment, circumambulating the House. They said: Whom does he resemble? He said: Urwah ibn Masud al-Thaqafi. And I saw Musa ibn Imran, a dark-skinned, slender man among the people, as if from the men of Shanua. And I saw the Dajjal. We said: Whom does he resemble, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan al-Mustaliqi."
"13355","13319 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah narrate from Abdullah ibn Wahb, that Uthman said to Ibn Umar: Go and be a judge. He said: Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No, go and judge among people. He said: Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No, I insist upon you that you go and judge. He said: Do not hasten; did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought refuge in a strong refuge? He said: Yes. He said: Then I seek refuge in Allah from being a judge. He said: What prevents you, when your father used to judge? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is a judge and judges out of ignorance will be among the people of Hell, and whoever is a knowledgeable judge and judges with truth or justice will ask to escape with barely enough. So what hope remains after this? Abu al-Qasim said: This Abdullah ibn Wahb is in my view Abdullah ibn Wahb ibn Zamaa, and Allah knows best."
"13356","13320 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muti narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have obtained of your world nothing except your women."
"13357","13321 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Abbad ibn Maysarah al-Minqari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse while upon the pulpit: And they did not estimate Allah with an estimation due to Him, to the end of the verse, and the pulpit shook thus and thus - meaning the pulpit trembled."
"13358","13322 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads a blind man forty steps, Paradise becomes due for him."
"13359","13323 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir say: A man met Ibn Umar while he was upon a young she-camel not worth ten dirhams, and said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, upon this you perform Hajj? He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not abandon Hajj, even upon a young she-camel worth ten dirhams. By Allah, nothing of my mounts was present except it, and I would not abandon Hajj."
"13360","13324 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Fulayh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, said: I have turned my face to the One Who originated the heavens and the earth, upright, a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. Glory be to You, O Allah, with Your praise, blessed is Your Name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You. Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice, my living and my dying, are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, without partner to Him, and with that I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims."
"13361","13325 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Musa ibn Abi Muslim, that he asked Ibn Umar about halting at al-Muhassab. He said: It is Sunnah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar halted there."
"13362","13326 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar Rustah narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Nafi ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Farwah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are best? He said: The best of them in character."
"13363","13327 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim informed us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit saying: The Compeller takes His heavens and His earth in His hands. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) closed his hand and kept closing and opening it, then said: He says: I am the Most Merciful, I am the King, where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swayed to his right and to his left, until I looked at the pulpit shaking from its lowest part, until I would say: Is it falling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"13364","13328 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Madini narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarrat, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution well, then goes out to the mosque with nothing bringing him out except prayer, his left foot keeps erasing a sin and the other writes a good deed, until he enters the mosque."
"13365","13329 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered Makkah, said: O Allah, do not make our deaths therein until You take us out of it."
"13366","13330 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ibrahim ibn Hatib, from his father and his uncle, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw the crescent, said: O Allah, bring it upon us with security and faith, safety and Islam, and success for what You love and approve; our Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"13367","13331 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I wore a lower garment rattling. He said: Who is this? I said: Abdullah. He said: If you are Abdullah, then raise your lower garment. So I raised my lower garment to the middle of the shins, and his lower wrap remained so until he died."
"13368","13332 - Ahmad ibn al-Khadir al-Khuzai al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Abu Ismah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the decisive sins were revealed, like His saying: Those who consume the wealth of orphans unjustly, to the end of the verse, and like: Those who consume usury, and like His saying: Whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, he said: We used to testify against whoever did any of this that he is in Hell. Then when His saying was revealed: Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be set up with Him and forgives what is less than that for whom He wills, we refrained from testifying, and we feared for them because of what Allah made due for them."
"13369","13333 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati and Muhammad ibn Hunayn al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Dawud ibn Rushaydin narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Ubulli, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every beast among the beasts of sea and land that has no blood which congeals has no zakat upon it."
"13370","13334 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has a creation whom He created for the needs of people; people hasten to them for their needs; those are the ones safe from the punishment of Allah."
"13371","13335 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"13372","13336 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me that his father narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them in the Farewell Hajj and said: Indeed Allah has made forbidden for you your blood and your wealth, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. He said that three times. Then he said: Look, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"13373","13337 - And with his chain, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise go to Paradise and the people of Hell go to Hell, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and Hell, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call: O people of Paradise, no death; and O people of Hell, no death. So the people of Paradise increase in joy added to their joy, and the people of Hell increase in sorrow added to their sorrow."
"13374","13338 - And from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to speak about the Farewell Hajj while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, and we did not know what the Farewell Hajj was. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as an orator, praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned the False Messiah, the Dajjal, and spoke at length about him. Then he said: Allah has not sent any prophet except that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Noah warned of him, and the prophets after him. And he will emerge among you; whatever is hidden from you of his affair, it is not hidden from you that he is blind in the right eye, as if it is a protruding grape."
"13375","13339 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in solitude, no one would travel by night alone."
"13376","13340 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"13377","13341 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard his father narrate from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If bad omen is in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house."
"13378","13342 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fever is from the blast of Hell, so extinguish it with water - or he said: cool it with water."
"13379","13343 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"13380","13344 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was given the keys of everything except the five: Indeed with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed Allah is Knowing, Aware."
"13381","13345 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking redress against his father. He said: He took from my wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you not know that you and your wealth are from your father's earning?"
"13382","13346 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a white-spotted ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. It will be said: O people of Paradise, do you know this? They will crane their necks and look. And it will be said: O people of Hell, do you know this? They will crane their necks and look. Then it will be slaughtered. Then it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death; and O people of Hell, eternity with no death."
"13383","13347 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knew that the most beloved of lands to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Makkah, and had my people not expelled me I would not have left. O Allah, place in our hearts love of Madinah like what You placed in our hearts of love of Makkah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never overlooked Madinah except that cheerfulness and joy were recognized in his face."
"13384","13348 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam narrated to us, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: We heard of the Farewell Hajj while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive among us, and we did not think it was a farewell from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned the Messiah at length in his mention, then mentioned of his affair what he wished to mention. Then he said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, never sent any prophet except that he warned his nation of the Messiah. Noah warned his nation of him, then the prophets after him, prophet by prophet. Lo, whoever of his affair is hidden from you - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hesitated to say it - then he said: Lo, whoever of his affair is hidden from you, it is not hidden from you that your Lord is not one-eyed, while he is one-eyed in the right eye, as if it is a protruding grape. Have I conveyed? They shouted from all sides: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness, three times. Then he said: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"13385","13349 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Haramalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, and he mentioned the Haruriyyah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game."
"13386","13350 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn Rishdin ibn Sad informed us, my father narrated to me, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Abdullah ibn Said, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah."
"13387","13351 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, Salih ibn Kaysan informed me that Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad informed him that Nafi informed him, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Envy is only - or as Allah willed him to say - for two traits: a man to whom Allah gave the Quran and he stands with it through hours of night and day, and a man to whom Allah gave wealth and he spends it."
"13388","13352 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted al-Zubayr the reach of his horse in a land called Thuwayr. He ran his horse until it stopped, then threw his whip and said: Give him where his whip reached."
"13389","13353 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he applied kohl, placed three in the right eye and two strokes in the left, making it odd."
"13390","13354 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Atiq ibn Yaqub al-Zubayri narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Plant much of the plantings of Paradise, for its water is sweet and its soil is good, so plant much of its plantings: There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"13391","13355 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my father - Ibn al-Ashjai gave us books - from his father, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spend the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and when he prayed Fajr he sat upon his mount and recited Talbiyah."
"13392","13356 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad informed me, from Ibn Wahb, from al-Umari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prostrate on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn."
"13393","13357 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"13394","13358 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Abu Musab al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm at Makkah and the people prostrated with him, until a man would raise something of the earth to his forehead and prostrate upon it, and until a man would prostrate upon another man."
"13395","13359 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no surah in the Mufassal, small or large, except that I have heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite it in the whole prayer."
"13396","13360 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami Sajjadah narrated to me, Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a woman used to borrow jewelry in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then withhold it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the woman repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and return what she has - while she was listening. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rise, O so-and-so, take her hand and cut it."
"13397","13361 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: While I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came and greeted him, then turned away from him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I love this man. He said: Have you informed him? I said: No. He said: Then inform that brother of yours. So I followed him and greeted him and took his shoulder and said: By Allah I love you for Allah. And he said: And I love you for Allah. And I said: Had the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not commanded me to inform you, I would not have done so."
"13398","13362 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten the dawn with Witr."
"13399","13363 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Uqbah Abu Masud al-Mujaddar narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced between horses, and gave precedence to the mature horses at the goal."
"13400","13364 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Umar ibn Yazid al-Sayyari narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to declare decisively against the killer, until: Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be set up with Him and forgives what is less than that for whom He wills, was revealed."
"13401","13365 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Jawhari narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Zibyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Mudabbar is from the third."
"13402","13366 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Zibyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tayammum is two strikes: a strike for the face, and a strike for the two hands up to the elbows."
"13403","13367 - Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Surah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr al-Shaybani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A lizard was eaten in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he found it distasteful, and we find distasteful what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found distasteful."
"13404","13368 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told while at al-Aqiq: You are in the blessed valley, or in a blessed plain."
"13405","13369 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My maternal uncle Uthman ibn Mazun sent me to bring him a quilt. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked his permission while he was at the Trench, and he permitted me and said to me: Whomever you meet, tell them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return. That was in severe cold. So I went out and met the people and told them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return. He said: By Allah, not even two or one turned toward me."
"13406","13370 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray on the day of the Confederates? He said: He used to pray in the belly of the ravine near a ruin there. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had permitted the people to leave, then commanded me to call them, so I called them."
"13407","13371 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from a journey and passed an open land and elevation, would say Takbir three times, then say: There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. Then he would say: Returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, to our Lord praising. Allah kept His promise true, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone."
"13408","13372 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that an army took spoils in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of food and honey, and no fifth was taken from them."
"13409","13373 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you pray in his mosque, and not follow after mosques."
"13410","13374 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Ubaydullah and Abdullah, the two sons of Umar, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of your names to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman."
"13411","13375 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Qilabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad Abu al-Jamal narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: There is no restriction of ihram upon the woman except in her face."
"13412","13376 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reserved al-Rabadhah for the charity livestock."
"13413","13377 - Abu Shaykh Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ajlan al-Asbahani and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about ablution after bathing, and he said: And what ablution is more complete than bathing?"
"13414","13378 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ajlan and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has altered."
"13415","13379 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls. And he claimed that Bilal used to call, and when Bilal descended, Ibn Umm Maktum would call."
"13416","13380 - Muhammad ibn Harun Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib: Those who disbelieved and barred from the way of Allah."
"13417","13381 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exited the mosque to al-Safa through the gate of Banu Makhzum."
"13418","13382 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go to the open prayer ground walking and return walking, and Abu Bakr and Umar did so."
"13419","13383 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, my father narrated to me, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said something hurtful to Umar, then said: Ask forgiveness for me, O my brother. Umar became angry, and he said that to him repeatedly, and Umar became angry. He mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they ended up with him and sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother asks you to seek forgiveness for him and you do not do so. He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, there is no time he asks me except that I seek forgiveness for him, and there is none of Allah's creation after you more beloved to me than him. Abu Bakr said: And I, by the One Who sent you with the truth, there is no one after you more beloved to me than him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not harm me regarding my Companion, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent me with guidance and the religion of truth and you said: You lie, while Abu Bakr said: You speak the truth. Had Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not named him a companion, I would have taken him as an intimate friend, but it is brotherhood in Allah. Lo, close every small door except the small door of Ibn Abi Quhafah."
"13420","13384 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man came to him greeting him and mentioned that he was going out on a journey. Ibn Umar said to him: Come, that I may bid you farewell as I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bid farewell to whoever went out. Then Abdullah said: I entrust to Allah your trust, your religion, and the seals of your deeds."
"13421","13385 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Tawbah al-Qazwini narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Preemption is in what boundaries have not fallen; when boundaries fall, there is no preemption."
"13422","13386 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Tawbah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the chiefs, he said: Let no man find anything in himself; I only take whom Jibril, peace be upon him, pointed to."
"13423","13387 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."
"13424","13388 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed the appointed places for their people and for whoever passes them intending Hajj and Umrah: for the people of Madinah, Dhu al-Hulayfah; for the people of Syria, al-Juhfah; and for the people of Najd, Qarn."
"13425","13389 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Nattah narrated to us, Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"13426","13390 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Judani narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings."
"13427","13391 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to say in the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Who is most entitled of people to this matter? We would say: Abu Bakr. Then we would say: What do you think, if Abu Bakr passes away, who will be most entitled of people to this matter? We would say: Umar ibn al-Khattab. Then we would say: What do you think, if Umar ibn al-Khattab passes away, who will be most entitled of people to this matter? We would say: Uthman."
"13428","13392 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while upon the pulpit: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"13429","13393 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever performs Hajj, let his last contact be with the House, except menstruating women, whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exempted."
"13430","13394 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fear prayer is that the imam stands with a group of people with him and they prostrate one prostration, while a group stands between them and the enemy. Then those who prostrated with their commander leave and take the place of those who have not prayed, and those who have not prayed advance and pray with their commander one prostration. Then their commander leaves, having completed his prayer, and each of the two groups prays for its own prayer one prostration by itself. If the fear is more severe than that, then on foot and mounted - meaning by prostration, a rakah."
"13431","13395 - Muhammad ibn Fada al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Budayl al-Yami narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Maghrib: Say, O you disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"13432","13396 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon twice, with a sitting between them."
"13433","13397 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Zakat al-Fitr upon every Muslim, free and slave, young and old: a sa of dates, or a sa of barley."
"13434","13398 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ata narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah grasps the heavens in His right hand, and the earths in His hand - I think he said: the other - then says: I am the King."
"13435","13399 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting, and gave the cupper his wage; had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."
"13436","13400 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring and wore it on his right hand."
"13437","13401 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Zayd al-Sudai narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, give us rain."
"13438","13402 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw no harm in silk brocade and silk for women."
"13439","13403 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."
"13440","13404 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed facing a camel."
"13441","13405 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Bahram al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to let his turban hang between his shoulders."
"13442","13406 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Taqi al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad al-Kufi narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and he wishes him to break his fast, let him break it, unless his fast is Ramadan, or making up Ramadan, or a vow."
"13443","13407 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Jews brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man and a woman of theirs who had committed adultery. He said to them: What do you do with one among you who commits adultery? They said: We beat them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you find in the Torah? They said: We find nothing in it. Abdullah ibn Salam said to them: You lie; in the Torah is stoning, so bring the Torah and recite if you are truthful. The Torah was brought, and their learned reader who had studied it placed his palm over the verse of stoning and kept reading what was below his hand and what was beyond it, without reading the verse of stoning. Abdullah pulled his hand away onto the verse of stoning and said: What is this? When they saw that, they said: It is stoning. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded regarding them both, and they were stoned where funerals are found. Abdullah said: I saw her companion bending over her to shield her from the stones."
"13444","13408 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to say: It has been forbidden to steep unripe dates and ripe dates together, and dates and raisins together."
"13445","13409 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Thabit al-Madani Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer at sunrise and at sunset."
"13446","13410 - al-Hasan ibn Alluyah al-Qattan narrated to us, Ali ibn Siyabah al-Kufi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept the Trench concealed except from six men: four of the Emigrants - Talhah, al-Zubayr, Ali, and Sad - and of the Ansar, Abu Dujanah and al-Harith ibn al-Simmah."
"13447","13411 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"13448","13412 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head in the Farewell Hajj."
"13449","13413 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samayda al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a fasting person has nothing from his fasting but hunger and thirst, and how many a night-praying person has nothing from his standing but sleeplessness."
"13450","13414 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is sufficient sin for a man to waste those whom he maintains."
"13451","13415 - Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a small mat and prostrate upon it."
"13452","13416 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Jubayr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed in a battle he fought by a slain woman and forbade killing women and children."
"13453","13417 - Yahya ibn Muhammad al-KhuttAli narrated to us, Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to approach two men while they are conversing privately, except with their permission."
"13454","13418 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj al-Hashimi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to turbans, for they are the mark of the angels, and let them hang behind your backs."
"13455","13419 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"13456","13420 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar, when he wished to enter ihram, would come to Dhu al-Hulayfah and spend the night. When morning came he mounted his camel, and when it stood straight with him he would recite Talbiyah, and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so."
"13457","13421 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, from his father, he said: Nafi wrote to me that Ibn Umar said: The flesh of domestic donkeys was forbidden."
"13458","13422 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ismail ibn Masud narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our Syria; O Allah, bless our Yemen. He said it repeatedly. When it was the third or fourth time, they said: O Messenger of Allah, and our Iraq? He said: In it are earthquakes and tribulations, and from it rises the horn of Satan."
"13459","13423 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzad narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hamzah informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to kill dogs, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog."
"13460","13424 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Isa ibn Umar ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed itikaf, his bedding and bed would be placed for him at the Pillar of Repentance facing the qiblah, then he would lean upon it."
"13461","13425 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abdullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah has cherished ones among His creation whom He keeps alive in well-being, and when He takes them to His Paradise. Those are they over whom tribulations pass like portions of dark night, while they remain therein in well-being."
"13462","13426 - al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas al-Qurazi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harbi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, Musa ibn Uqbah, Abdullah ibn Umar, Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Saman, Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, and Burd ibn Sinan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment toward Najd, and Abdullah was among them. We took many camels as spoils, and our shares reached twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah gave us an extra camel each."
"13463","13427 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting Talbiyah when his mount stood straight with him."
"13464","13428 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzad narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over an adulteress who died in childbirth, and her child."
"13465","13429 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah Quhzad narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The woman divorced thrice is not lawful for her first husband until she marries another husband, he consummates with her, and she tastes of his sweetness."
"13466","13430 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to perform ablution three times three times, attributing that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13467","13431 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Baballutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar about Witr. He said: Pray Witr with one. The man said: I fear people will say it is al-Butayra. He said: The Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger - meaning: this is the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13468","13432 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Ibn Umar, he said: I have not seen anyone among people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more eminent than Muawiyah."
"13469","13433 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me in a Qubtiyyah garment, and clothed Usamah ibn Zayd in a striped silk robe. He looked and saw me trailing, so he came and took my shoulder and said: O Ibn Umar, everything of garments that touches the ground is in Hell. So I saw Ibn Umar wrapping to the middle of the shin."
"13470","13434 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd al-Faraidi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of houses to Allah is a house in which an orphan is honored."
"13471","13435 - Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Humran, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, ten good deeds are written for him for every letter. Whoever aids in a false dispute remains in the wrath of Allah until he desists. Whoever intercedes to block a hadd among the hudud of Allah has opposed Allah in His command. Whoever slanders a believing man or believing woman, Allah will confine him in the mire of Khabal on the Day of Resurrection, until he exits from what he said, and he will not exit."
"13472","13436 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: All flies are in Hell except the bee. And he used to forbid killing them and burning food. Sufyan said: It is likely that burning food refers to the land of the enemy."
"13473","13437 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while upon the pulpit saying: The Judge takes His heavens and His earths in His hand. And he closed his hand, closing and opening them, then said: I am the Compeller, where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swayed to his right and to his left, until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lowest part, until I would say: Is it falling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"13474","13438 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar and al-Thawri informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Touching the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner effaces sins thoroughly."
"13475","13439 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi narrated to me, from his father, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I see you crowding at these two Corners. He said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Touching them both effaces sins."
"13476","13440 - And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates this House seven times, counting it, a good deed is written for him for every step, a sin is expiated from him, a rank is raised for him, and it equals freeing a slave."
"13477","13441 - And I heard him say: Whoever drinks wine, no prayer will be accepted from him - or Allah will not accept prayer from him - for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah turns to him. If he returns, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah turns to him. If he returns, no prayer will be accepted from him, and it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the river of Khabal. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the river of Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Hell."
"13478","13442 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of Mazin, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Three at whom Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection: the one who reminds of his gift, the one who trails his lower garment out of pride, and the addict of wine. It was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the addict of wine? He said: Persistence upon it."
"13479","13443 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Tufayl ibn Sinan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: I heard a man say to Ibn Umar: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I jest, but I say only the truth? He said: Yes."
"13480","13444 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Khalifah ibn Khayyat al-Usfuri narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, narrated to us, from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar crowding severely at the two Corners, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crowding at them, and I heard him say: He places no foot nor raises it except that a good deed is written for him thereby."
"13481","13445 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed me, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty nights. If he repents, Allah turns to him - he said it three times - and if he returns, it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the river of Khabal. It was said: What is the river of Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Hell."
"13482","13446 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do I see you touching the two Corners and never leaving them, while Ibn Umar used to do so? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Touching them both effaces sins."
"13483","13447 - And I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates this House for a week, it counts for him as freeing a slave."
"13484","13448 - And I heard him say: Whoever drinks wine in this world, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty nights. If he repents, Allah turns to him. If he returns, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty nights. If he repents, Allah turns to him. If he returns, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty nights. If he repents, Allah turns to him. If he drinks it a fourth time, it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the clay of Khabal. It was said: What is the clay of Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of Hell."
"13485","13449 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The measure is the measure of the people of Madinah, and the weight is the weight of the people of Makkah."
"13486","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashi both narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us. (H) And Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Tawus, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about nabidh (fermented drink) made in an earthen jar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh made in the jar. And Sulayman ibn Harb said in his narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared it unlawful."
"13487","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, in the year 211, by dictation: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, they both said: We heard Tawus saying: By Allah, a man came to Ibn Umar and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid nabidh of the jar? He said: Yes."
"13488","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Sulayman Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Tawus, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid nabidh of the jar? He said: Yes. Tawus swore to us by Allah that he heard it from Ibn Umar."
"13489","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Bakkar ibn Wayhak, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he asked Tawus about drinks, and he informed him, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (nabidh in) the earthen jar and the gourd."
"13490","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that a man came to him and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid making nabidh in the jar and the gourd? He said: Yes."
"13491","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared nabidh of the jar unlawful."
"13492","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he heard Ibn Umar being asked about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? He said: Yes. He said: He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him the news, and he commanded him to take her back. He said: I did not hear him add anything beyond that."
"13493","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us: Abd al-Nur ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have become infatuated against Ammar; he calls them to Paradise and they call him to the Fire."
"13494","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Himsi narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Tawbah al-Numayri, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the believer's honor with Allah is the cleanliness of his garment and his contentment with little."
"13495","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Umar; and Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a race between horses: he sent the trained horses from al-Hayfa', with their finish line at Thaniyyat al-Wada', and he raced the horses that had not been trained, with their course from the Thaniyyah to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."
"13496","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Maqabiri narrated to us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard Tawus saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to depart (from Mina) until his last contact is with the House, except menstruating women; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to depart."
"13497","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Tawus, who said: I heard Ibn Umar narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The night prayer is two by two, and when you fear the dawn, then one."
"13498","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is not lawful for a man who gives a gift or grants a present to take it back, except a father regarding what he gives his child. The likeness of one who gives a gift then takes it back is like the dog: it eats, and when it is full and satisfied it returns to its vomit."
"13499","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, in a raised report, he said: Fruit is not to be sold until its soundness appears."
"13500","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: Dung-eating animals (al-jallalah) were forbidden."
"13501","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, answer him; whoever does you a kindness, reward him; and if you find nothing with which to reward him, supplicate for him until he sees that you have rewarded him."
"13502","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us. (H) And Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, they both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"13503","Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us: Yahya Abu Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fly is in the Fire. And he forbade killing bees, and burning food in the land of the enemy."
"13504","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee."
"13505","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, they both said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Bishr, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caller to prayer (mu'adhdhin) is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry bears witness for him."
"13506","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us. (H) And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of my shoulder and said: Be in this world as a stranger or as a passer-by."
"13507","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Layth, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give women permission to go to the mosque at night. His son said: By Allah, we will not give them permission, lest they take that as a pretext for mischief. So he said: May Allah deal with you as you deserve; you hear me say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and you say: No. Layth said in his narration: And let them go out unattired."
"13508","Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not forbid women the mosques at night. His son said: By Allah, we shall forbid them. So he stretched out his hand and struck him, and said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you say what you say."
"13509","Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Amr ibn Hakam narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The moon split in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13510","Ahmad ibn Hammuyah Abu Sayyar al-Tustari narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Musa Abu Ghassan al-Sukkari al-Razi narrated to us: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not witness any of your pastimes except horse-racing and archery."
"13511","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: O Messenger of Allah, if only we took the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. Then it was revealed: {And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer}."
"13512","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us: Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us: Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from this and leave this - meaning he trims from his mustache area and leaves his beard."
"13513","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and masculine women."
"13514","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki' narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever disowns his child to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before all witnesses, measure for measure."
"13515","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ali al-Za'farani narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid and al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stoning the pillars (ramy al-jimar), what reward is in it? I heard him saying: You will find that with your Lord when you need it most."
"13516","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah al-Razi narrated to us: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Razi, from Husayn, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, answer him; and whoever presents you with a trotter as a gift, accept it."
"13517","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us: Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Fudayl ibn Amr, from Abu al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the night (Isha) prayer until those who pray had prayed, those wakeful had woken, the sleepers had slept, and those keeping night vigil had prayed tahajjud. Then he came out and said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to pray at this time, or this prayer, or words to that effect."
"13518","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us. (H) And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, they both said: Imran ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The people of the Fire will grow large in the Fire until the distance between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years, the thickness of one's skin is forty cubits, and his molar tooth is greater than Mount Uhud. Their wording is one."
"13519","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand up for the funeral of a Jew that passed by him."
"13520","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, they both said: Isra'il narrated to us: Abu Yahya al-Qattat narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to follow a funeral procession accompanied by wailing."
"13521","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation."
"13522","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man called the second call (thawwaba) at Zuhr and Asr, so he said: An innovation; take us out, for this is an innovation."
"13523","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us: Qabisah ibn Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came as pilgrims, and he said: O people, enter ihram for Umrah, except whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, for Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"13524","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban narrated to us: Mindal narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"13525","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, that a man came to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him: How are you and Abu Unays - meaning al-Dahhak ibn Qays? He said: We and he, when we meet him we say to him what he likes, and when we turn away from him we say otherwise. He said: That is what we, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to count as hypocrisy."
"13526","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisia narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ata' narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked him about fadikh. He said: What is fadikh? He said: We crush unripe dates, then add ripe dates with them, then leave it and drink it. He said: That is faduakh. Wine has been forbidden, and most of the drink of theirs that you mention is that."
"13527","Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked him about fadikh. He said: What is fadikh? He said: Unripe dates and ripe dates. He said: That is faduakh. Wine has been forbidden, and it was our drink."
"13528","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine and puts it in his belly, no prayer will be accepted from him for seven (days); if he dies in that state he dies a disbeliever. If it robs his mind of any of the obligatory duties, no prayer will be accepted from him for forty days; if he dies in that state he dies a disbeliever."
"13529","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri and Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, they both said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Say: He is Allah, the One} equals a third of the Qur'an, and {Say: O disbelievers} equals a fourth of the Qur'an. And he used to recite them in the two rak'ahs of Fajr, and he said: These two rak'ahs contain the most coveted rewards of a lifetime."
"13530","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Layth ibn Hammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the gentlest of you in shouldering (shoulder-to-shoulder) in prayer."
"13531","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and shook his hand, and he did not withdraw his hand from the man's hand until the man withdrew his hand. Then he said to him: O Messenger of Allah, what of Uthman? He said: He is a man of Paradise."
"13532","Ahmad ibn Rashdin narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Ansari narrated to us: al-Layth ibn bint al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, he said: my grandmother A'ishah bint Yunus, the wife of al-Layth, narrated to me, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me in my life."
"13533","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us: Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever performs Hajj and visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me in my life."
"13534","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to follow a funeral in which there is wailing."
"13535","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan narrated to us: Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were forbidden - or we were prohibited - to pray in an elevated (ornate, towering) mosque."
"13536","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father: Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O son of Adam, guarantee Me two rak'ahs at the beginning of the day and I will suffice you its end."
"13537","Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Tawwazi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Yahya al-Dibili narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra' narrated to us: Jabir ibn Yahya al-Hadrami informed us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drags his lower garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13538","And I heard him saying: Do not leave the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer, for in them are most coveted rewards."
"13539","And I heard him saying: Do not disown your child, lest Allah disgrace you before all creatures as you disgraced him in this world."
"13540","And I heard him saying: Do not die while you owe a debt, for there it is only good deeds and evil deeds; there is no dinar nor dirham there - recompense and settlement - and He wrongs no one."
"13541","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let none of you prevent his family from coming to the mosque."
"13542","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, on the day of the Conquest, the meat and milk of dung-eating camels (al-jallalah)."
"13543","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Mada'ini narrated to us: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Warqa' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It does not befit a believer to humiliate himself. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself? He said: By exposing himself to a trial he cannot bear."
"13544","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us. (H) And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar from Makkah to Madinah and did not hear him narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except one hadith. He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: There is a tree among trees whose likeness is that of the Muslim man. I wanted to say: It is the palm tree, but I looked and I was the youngest of the people, so I stayed silent."
"13545","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uqal al-Harrani narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us: Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives to perform tamattu' (Umrah joined with Hajj), and he ordered departure for them."
"13546","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Tamim ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House (Ka'bah) with al-Fadl with him, while Bilal stood at the door."
"13547","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us: Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd Manaf, let me not know you preventing anyone from circling this House at any hour of night or day."
"13548","Al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us: Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Karim, that is Ibn Rashid - he narrated with isnad only this hadith - and another narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar said: I was given something of it; I know of no one given it except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning marital intercourse."
"13549","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Among trees there is a tree like the believing man. I wanted to say: It is the palm tree, but I looked at the faces of the people and I was the youngest of them in age. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the palm tree."
"13550","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The likeness of the believer is that of the palm tree; whatever you take from it benefits you."
"13551","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating the heart (jummar) of a palm tree."
"13552","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Asbat ibn Azrah, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sneezed and praised Allah, so they said: May Allah have mercy on you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."
"13553","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Tell me of a tree whose likeness is that of the believer. People began mentioning trees of the valley, and it occurred to me that it is the palm tree, so I wanted to speak but I saw elders among the people and felt shy of that. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the palm tree."
"13554","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid al-A'raj al-Shanni, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House - and pilgrimage to this House, twice."
"13555","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, he said: I heard Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrating from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the sun was over Qu'ayqi'an after Asr, and he said: Your lifespans compared to the lifespans of those who passed are only like what remains of this day compared to what has passed of it."
"13556","Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the believer is that of the palm tree."
"13557","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was eating jummar with the people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among trees there is a tree like the Muslim man. He said: The people fell silent until I almost asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though I was the youngest of the people. Then he said: It is the palm tree."
"13558","Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given five things no prophet before me was given: I was sent to all people, the red and the black, while each prophet was sent only to his town; I was aided with terror - my enemy fears me at a month's distance; war booty was given to me; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification; and I was given intercession, which I have stored up for my community."
"13559","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us: my father narrated to us. (H) And Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi' al-Naysaburi informed us, they both said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four Umrahs, one of them in Rajab."
"13560","Abu Mulayl Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi al-Kufi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Harasah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Duha prayer is an innovation."
"13561","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us: Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the mosque of al-Khayf are the graves of seventy prophets."
"13562","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Mujahid, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar, I and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and Urwah asked him: In which month did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform Umrah? He said: He used to perform Umrah in Rajab."
"13563","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: al-Thawri informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than twenty-five times - or he said: more than twenty times - reciting in the two rak'ahs of Fajr {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"13564","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the two rak'ahs of Fajr {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"13565","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah twice before he performed Hajj. That reached A'ishah and she said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four Umrahs; Abdullah ibn Umar knew of them - one Umrah along with his Hajj."
"13566","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever presents you with a trotter as a gift, accept it."
"13567","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon us the neighbor until we thought he would make him an heir."
"13568","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Wadi'i Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: Jandal ibn Waliq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering seeking Allah's forgiveness a hundred times, saying: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, and turn to me; indeed You are the Most Relenting, the Most Merciful."
"13569","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, they both said: Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Mujahid, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: What do you say about Ali, may Allah be pleased with him? He said: That is his house. He said: What do you say about Uthman? He said: What can I say about a man who committed a sin between him and his Lord and He pardoned him, and committed a sin between you and him and you killed him?"
"13570","Al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ashras ibn Hassan al-Asadi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."
"13571","Al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Hassan, that is the brother of Ashras, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that he was leaning against the chamber of A'ishah when he was asked: In which month did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform Umrah? He said: In Rajab."
"13572","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Misri narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Mu'alla, that is al-Kindi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as one of ten, and a man from the Ansar came and said: O Prophet of Allah, who are the most astute and firm of people? He said: Those who remember death most and prepare most for death before it descends; those are the astute - they have carried off the honor of this world and the Hereafter."
"13573","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: He said to me: Love for Allah, hate for Allah, befriend for Allah, and oppose for Allah, for the friendship of Allah is not attained except by that, and a man does not taste faith - even if his prayer and fasting are many - until he is so. People's brotherhood has come to be over worldly matters, and that avails its people nothing. He said: And Ibn Umar said to me: When you wake in the morning do not think of the evening, and when you reach the evening do not think of the morning; take from your health for your sickness and from your life for your death, for you, O Abdullah - meaning himself - do not know what your name will be tomorrow. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of part of my body and said: Be in this world a stranger or a passer-by, and count yourself among the people of the graves."
"13574","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of part of my body and said: O Ibn Umar, be in this world as a stranger or a passer-by, and count yourself among the people of the graves."
"13575","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever presents you a gift, accept it."
"13576","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever presents you with a foreleg or a trotter as a gift, accept it."
"13577","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Huraym ibn Mis'ar al-Tirmidhi narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is that of the perfume-seller: if you sit with him he benefits you, if you walk with him he benefits you, and if you partner with him he benefits you."
"13578","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee."
"13579","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umar - or from Ibn Umar - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee. He used to forbid killing them and burning food."
"13580","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar and Ubayd ibn Umayr, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Flies are in the Fire except the bee. So they used to dislike killing it and burning food."
"13581","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn bint Rashdin ibn Sa'd al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Abu al-Muhayyah Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No townsman shall sell for a Bedouin; do not meet arriving caravans (to intercept trade); do not outbid one another to inflate prices; none of you shall propose over his brother's proposal; a woman shall not ask for her sister's divorce to empty what is in her bowl, for she has only what was written for her; and do not leave camels and sheep unmilked (to deceive buyers). Whoever buys an animal with withheld milk has two options: if he returns it, he returns it with a sa' of dates."
"13582","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to meet traders at the mouths of roads, and that a townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"13583","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara' narrated to us: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No townsman shall sell for a Bedouin, nor buy for him."
"13584","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: It was said to him: When we enter upon the rulers we say to them what we do not say to them when we leave them. He said: We used to count that as hypocrisy in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13585","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid, that is Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i, narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Tuhawi narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: While I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the shade in Madinah, and he was seeking Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, we came to a walled garden and looked inside, and he saw Ali sleeping on the ground, covered in dust. He said: I do not blame people for calling you Abu Turab. I saw Ali's face change and that weighed heavily. So he said: Shall I not please you, O Ali? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are my brother and my minister; you will settle my debt, fulfill my promise, and clear my liability. Whoever loves you during a life from me has fulfilled his vow; whoever loves you during a life from you after me, Allah will seal for him safety and faith; whoever loves you after me without having seen you, Allah will seal for him safety and faith and secure him on the day of the Greatest Terror; and whoever dies hating you, O Ali, dies the death of ignorance, and Allah will reckon him for what he did in Islam."
"13586","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us: Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first for whom I shall intercede on the Day of Resurrection are my household, then the nearest then the nearest of Quraysh, then the Ansar, then those who believed in me and followed me from Yemen, then the rest of the Arabs, then the non-Arabs. And the first for whom I intercede are the people of excellence."
"13587","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies in the morning shall not rest at midday except in his grave, and whoever dies in the evening shall not spend the night except in his grave."
"13588","Abdullah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muslim al-A'war, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade letting the lower garment hang (below the ankles)."
"13589","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah did not unleash upon Ad, of the wind by which they were destroyed, except the like of the place of a ring. It passed by the desert-dwellers and carried their livestock and property, lifting them between heaven and earth. When the townspeople saw the wind and what was in it, they said: This is a cloud bringing us rain. Then it cast the desert-dwellers and their livestock upon the townspeople."
"13590","Ahmad ibn al-Ja'd al-Washsha' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mu'adhdhin who seeks reward is like the martyr, floundering in his blood until he finishes his call to prayer; everything moist and dry bears witness for him, and when he dies no worms appear in his grave."
"13591","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il al-Nahdi narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Throne shook out of love for meeting Allah - Sa'd; and the last of them to come out of his grave was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Sa'd was squeezed in his grave with a squeeze, so I asked Allah to lighten it for him."
"13592","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us: Imran ibn Utaybah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warrior in the path of Allah and the pilgrim to the House of Allah are the delegation of Allah: He called them and they answered Him."
"13593","Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amrawayh al-Harawi narrated to us: al-Jarud ibn Yazid narrated to us: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord is Shy and Generous; He is shy to have the servant raise his hands and return them empty with no good in them. When one of you raises his hands, let him say: O Living One, there is no god but You, O Most Merciful of the merciful - three times - then when he lowers his hands, let him pass that good over his face."
"13594","Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: Emigration (hijrah) ended after the Conquest."
"13595","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Subayh al-Asadi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Imran ibn Ammar, from Abu Idris: Mujahid narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever parts from Ali parts from me, and whoever parts from me parts from Allah."
"13596","Al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Rummani al-Massisi narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Sa'id Abu Khaythamah narrated to me: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Fitr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who gives out of plenty is not better than the one who takes when he is in need."
"13597","Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Nahik al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him pay the zakah of his wealth; whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him speak good or remain silent; and whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him honor his guest."
"13598","Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever says: Praise be to Allah, before Whose majesty everything humbles itself; praise be to Allah, before Whose might everything is low; praise be to Allah, before Whose dominion everything submits; praise be to Allah, to Whose power everything surrenders - saying it seeking what is with Him - Allah writes for him a thousand good deeds, raises him a thousand degrees, and appoints seventy thousand angels seeking forgiveness for him until the Day of Resurrection."
"13599","Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Duha prayer is an innovation, yet a fine innovation."
"13600","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'ahs of Fajr {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"13601","Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Ma'mar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us: Amir ibn Mudrik narrated to us: Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not forbid the maidservants of Allah the mosques of Allah."
"13602","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Mujahid, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: Two men came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one from the Ansar and the other from Thaqif, and the Ansari preceded him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Thaqafi: O brother of Thaqif, the Ansari has preceded you. The Ansari said: I defer to him, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said to him: O brother of Thaqif, ask about your need, and if you wish I shall tell you what you came asking about. He said: That you do so is dearer to me. He said: You ask me about your prayer, your bowing, your prostration, and your fasting, saying: What is in it for me? He said: Yes, by Him Who sent you with the truth. He said: Pray at the beginning of the night and its end, and sleep in its middle. He said: What if I pray in its middle? He said: Then you are so. He said: When you stand for prayer and bow, place your hands on your knees and spread your fingers, then raise your head until every limb returns to its joint; when you prostrate, press your forehead firmly on the ground and do not peck; and fast the white nights, the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth. Then he turned to the Ansari and said: Ask about your need, and if you wish I shall tell you. He said: That is dearer to me. He said: You came asking me about your leaving your house heading for the Sacred House, saying: What is in it for me? And you came asking about your standing at Arafah, saying: What is in it for me? And about your stoning the pillars, saying: What is in it for me? And about your circling the House, saying: What is in it for me? And about your shaving your head, saying: What is in it for me? He said: Yes, by Him Who sent you with the truth. He said: As for your leaving your house heading for the House, for every step your mount treads Allah writes for you a good deed and erases from you an evil deed. As for your standing at Arafah, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of them to the angels, saying: These are My servants; they have come to Me disheveled and dusty from every deep valley, hoping for My mercy and fearing My punishment, though they have not seen Me - how would it be if they saw Me? Even if you had sins like the sands of Alij, or like the days of this world, or like the drops of the sky, Allah would wash them from you. As for your stoning the pillars, it is stored up for you. As for your shaving your head, for every hair that falls you have a good deed. And when you circle the House, you emerge from your sins as the day your mother bore you."
"13603","Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Qarani narrated to us: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: Bishr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mujahid narrated to me, from his father, from the Abadilah - Abdullah ibn Umar, Abdullah ibn al-Abbas, Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, and Abdullah ibn Amr - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The storyteller (qass) awaits death, the listener awaits mercy, the merchant awaits provision, the hoarder awaits the curse, and the wailing woman and the women around her - upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"13604","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Mujahid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and spread his right palm and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans; nothing is added to them nor subtracted from them. Then he spread his left palm and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful, for the people of the Fire, with their names, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans; nothing is added to them nor subtracted from them."
"13605","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, the author of the Maghazi, narrated to me: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch the Yemeni Corner and the (Black) Stone, and would not touch any besides them."
"13606","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Warqa' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Give women permission (to go) to the mosques at night."
"13607","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi and Abu Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn A'idh al-Dimashqi narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us: al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: I set out for a raid, I and a man with me, and Abdullah ibn Umar saw us off. When he was about to part from us he said: It would please me what you two have been given, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When something is entrusted to Allah, He preserves it; and I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the seals of your deeds."
"13608","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar al-Makki, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed i'tikaf and addressed the people, saying: When one of you stands in prayer he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let each of you know what he converses with his Lord about, and let none of you raise his voice over another in recitation during prayer."
"13609","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is praying, let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him; if he refuses, let him fight him, for with him is the companion (qarin)."
"13610","Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Duhaym al-Kufi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Subayh narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice in talbiyah when his mount rose with him."
"13611","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed as miqat: for the people of Madinah, Dhu al-Hulayfah; for the people of Syria, al-Juhfah; for the people of Najd, Qarn; and for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam."
"13612","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said: To proceed."
"13613","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Wiqa' ibn Iyas al-Walibi, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"13614","Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz narrated to us: Abu Ma'mar Salih ibn Harb narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Did you witness the Pledge of Ridwan with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. I said: What was he wearing? He said: A cotton shirt, a stuffed cloak, a wrap, and a sword. And I saw al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani standing over his head, lifting the branches of the tree from over his head, while the people pledged allegiance to him."
"13615","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his voice in talbiyah when his mount stood upright with him."
"13616","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Isma'il al-Talqani narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not disfigure the face, for the son of Adam was created in the image of the Most Merciful, exalted is He."
"13617","Al-Husayn ibn Bahan al-Askari narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us. (H) And Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah narrated to us, they both said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we travel and meet people who say there is no decree (qadar). He said: When you meet such, tell them that Ibn Umar is free of them. We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when there came to him a man with a handsome face, sweet scent, and clean garment. He said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah; may I draw near you? He said: Draw near. He drew near a little, repeating that several times, until his knees touched the knees of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He said: Bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, fasting Ramadan, and bathing from major impurity. He said: If I do that, am I a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken truly. He said: What is faith? He said: Faith is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, Paradise, the Fire, the Resurrection, and the decree - its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter - from Allah. He said: If I do that, am I a believer? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken truly. He said: What is excellence (ihsan)? He said: To worship Allah as though you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, am I a doer of excellence? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken truly. We said: We never saw a man more handsome of face, sweeter of scent, or more reverent toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet saying to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You have spoken truly. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the man. So we stood up, and I stood on one of the roads of Madinah, but we saw nothing. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know who this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is Jibreel, peace be upon him, teaching you the rites of your religion. He never came to me in any form but I recognized him, except this form."
"13618","Al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a Bedouin approached. When he drew near, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Where are you heading? He said: To my family. He said: Do you care for some good? He said: What is it? He said: That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said: Who bears witness to what you say? He said: This tree. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called it, while it was at the bank of the valley, and it came forward plowing the earth until it stood before him. He called it to witness three times and it bore witness that he is as he said. Then it returned to its planting place, and the Bedouin returned to his people and said: If they follow me I shall bring them to you; otherwise I shall return to you and stay with you."
"13619","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-A'yan Muhammad ibn Abi Attab narrated to us: Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: There was a time upon us when none of us deemed himself more entitled to the dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother, and I am in a time when the dinar and dirham are dearer to us than our Muslim brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people are miserly with the dinar and dirham, abandon jihad in the path of Allah, cling to the tails of cattle, and trade with inah (usurious buy-back sales), Allah will unleash upon them a calamity He will not lift until they return."
"13620","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Farra' al-Naysaburi narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Muslim narrated to us: Bahr ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Furafisah, from al-A'mash, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: Had I not heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except once and once and once - he counted seven times - I would not have narrated it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Three shall be upon dunes of musk on the Day of Resurrection, untouched by grief, unafraid when people are afraid: a man who learned the Qur'an and stood by it, seeking thereby the face of Allah and what is with Him; a man who calls to the five prayers every day and night, seeking thereby the face of Allah and what is with Him; and a slave whom the bondage of this world did not prevent from obeying his Lord."
"13621","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, they both said: Mu'alla ibn Mahdi al-Mawsili narrated to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: There was a time upon us when none of us deemed himself more entitled to the dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother, until at the end of it we woke to find the dinar and dirham dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people are miserly with the dinar and dirham, trade with inah, and follow the tails of cattle, Allah will send upon them humiliation He will not lift from them until they return to their religion."
"13622","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: Selling war booty was forbidden until it is divided."
"13623","Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) twenty-five times, and he used to recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr and the two rak'ahs before Maghrib {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"13624","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamadani narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Muslim al-Jurjani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Sayf narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Ata', from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May Allah curse whoever reviles my Companions."
"13625","Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us: Abu Umar al-Darir and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."
"13626","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Habib al-Qanawi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn al-Sammak Abu Muhammad narrated to us: Ata' ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he sought Bilal to call the adhan for them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a man, who called the adhan in Bilal's place. After that he wanted to call the iqamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only the one who called the adhan calls the iqamah."
"13627","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Rashid al-Sammak narrated to us: Ata' ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: Two festivals coincided in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the day of Fitr and Friday. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in the Eid prayer, then turned to them with his face and said: O people, you have attained good and reward; we shall gather (for Friday), so whoever wishes to gather with us, let him gather, and whoever wishes to return to his family, let him return."
"13628","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick (siwak) at every prayer."
"13629","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sit for any hour of the night without passing the siwak over his mouth."
"13630","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Massisi narrated to us: Dawud ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Rashid al-Sammak narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fewest of my community are those who reach seventy."
"13631","13595 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated, Afif ibn Salim narrated, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man from Abyssinia came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask and seek understanding. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you have been favored over us in forms, colors, and prophethood; tell me, if I believe in what you believe in and do what you do, will I be with you in Paradise? He said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the whiteness of the black man will surely be seen in Paradise from a distance of a thousand years of travel. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, it will be for him a covenant with Allah, and whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, one hundred thousand good deeds and twenty-four good deeds will be written for him. A man said: How can one perish after this, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds that, if placed upon a mountain, would weigh it down, then a blessing from the blessings of Allah will stand forth and will almost consume all of that, unless Allah extends him with His mercy. And this surah was sent down: {Has there come upon man a period of time when he was nothing mentioned} up to His saying: {and a great kingdom}. The Abyssinian said: Will my two eyes really see what your two eyes see in Paradise? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Then he wept until his soul departed. Ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lowering him into his grave with his own hand."
"13632","13596 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Habib al-Muallim, from Ata, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah in Rajab."
"13633","13597 - Jafar ibn Bujayr al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated, Amir ibn Yasaf narrated, from al-Nadr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, one hundred thousand good deeds and twenty-four thousand good deeds will be written for him, and whoever says: There is no god but Allah, it will be for him a covenant with Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"13634","13598 - Muhammad ibn Qada al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad al-Muthanna narrated, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated, Husam ibn Misakk narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not wake in an hour of the night without passing the siwak over his mouth."
"13635","13599 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated, Imran ibn Anas al-Makki narrated, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mention the good qualities of your dead, and refrain from their faults."
"13636","13600 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated, al-Yasa ibn Talhah narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once led us in prayer, and when he raised his head from bowing he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him. A man behind him said: Our Lord, and to You belongs praise, abundant, good, blessed therein. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said three times: Who was speaking just now? The man said: I was, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I saw more than thirty angels hastening to it, which of them would write it first."
"13637","13601 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated, Khalid narrated, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in a dream as though upon his forearms were two bracelets of gold, so he blew them and they flew away. He said: They are the two liars of my ummah, the man of Yemen and the man of Yamamah, and they will not harm my ummah at all."
"13638","13602 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from his father, from Hanash, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I came early going to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Abu al-Hasan came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Come near me, O Abu al-Hasan. He kept bringing him near until he took his ear, then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to his left until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head as though startled, and said: The wicked one has knocked at the door with his hearing. He said: Go, O Abu al-Hasan, and lead him as a sheep is led to its milker. Then I saw Ali come with al-Hakam, holding him by his ear and both sides of his jaw together, until he stood him before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed him three times, then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Sit aside, until some people of the Muhajirun and Ansar went to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him, then said: This one will oppose the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from his loins will come tribulations whose smoke will reach the sky. A man from the Muslims said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; he is too small and too lowly for that to come from him. He said: Yes indeed, and some of you on that day will be his partisans."
"13639","13603 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Mutamir narrated, from his father, from Hanash, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not look to their needs, Allah will not look to his need until he looks to their needs."
"13640","13604 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, Mutamir narrated, from his father, from Hanash, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his palm like this, as though measuring a span: Whoever separates from the congregation of the Muslims by a span has removed from his neck the yoke of Islam, and the dissenters with their banners will take them on the Day of Resurrection from behind their backs, and whoever dies without an imam of the congregation dies a death of ignorance."
"13641","13605 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik al-Halabi narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not revile your dead, for reviling them is not lawful."
"13642","13606 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - and he visited Abu Salamah while he was ill, and heard the words of Umm Salamah while she was weeping, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held back from entering when he heard her bewailing him with the Book of Allah, saying: {And the agony of death comes in truth; that is what you used to avoid}. Then he entered, greeted, and said: May Allah compensate you, O Umm Salamah. When he came out with Abu Bakr with him, he said to him: I saw you, O Messenger of Allah, dislike entering because they wail. He said: I do not enter a house in which there is wailing, nor a black dog."
"13643","13607 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he came to a cloth merchant and bought from him a shirt for four dirhams, and went out wearing it, when a man from the Ansar met him and said: O Messenger of Allah, clothe me with a shirt; may Allah clothe you with garments of Paradise. So he removed the shirt and clothed him with it. Then he returned to the shop owner and bought from him a shirt for four dirhams, and two dirhams remained with him, when he saw a slave girl on the road weeping. He said: What makes you weep? She said: O Messenger of Allah, my family gave me two dirhams to buy flour with them, and they were lost. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the two remaining dirhams. Then she turned away weeping, so he called her and said: What makes you weep when you have taken the two dirhams? She said: I fear they will beat me. So he walked with her to her family and greeted, and they recognized his voice. Then he returned and greeted, then returned and greeted, then returned and greeted a third time, and they responded. He said: Did you hear the first greeting? They said: Yes, but we loved that you increase us in greeting. What has brought you, may our fathers and mothers be ransom for you? He said: This slave girl feared that you would beat her. Her owner said: She is free for the sake of Allah because of your walking with her. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave them glad tidings of goodness and Paradise, then said: Allah has blessed the ten: Allah clothed His Prophet with a shirt, and a man from the Ansar with a shirt, and Allah freed a slave from it, and I praise Allah, He who provided us this by His power."
"13644","13608 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Who will take this letter of mine to the tyrant of Rome? He presented that to them three times, then said: Who will go, and Paradise will be his? A man from the Ansar called Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Khaliq said: I will go with it, and Paradise will be mine if I perish short of that? He said: Yes, Paradise is yours if you deliver it, if you are killed, and if you perish, Allah has made Paradise obligatory for you. So he set out with the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he reached the tyrant. He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. Permission was given to him and he entered upon him. The tyrant of Rome recognized that he had come with the truth from a sent Prophet. Then he presented to him the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He gathered the Romans with him, then presented it to them, and they disliked what he brought. A man among them believed in it and was killed upon his belief. Then the man returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what had happened from him and of the killing of the man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said then: Allah will raise him as a nation alone - meaning that slain man."
"13645","13609 - And with his chain, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no believing servant who repents to Allah a month before death but Allah accepts from him, and nearer than that, and a day before his death, or an hour, when Allah knows repentance and sincerity from him, but Allah accepts from him."
"13646","13610 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day a man was placed in his grave: Two angels came to him and said to him: We will strike you one blow. He said to them: For what will you strike me? They struck him a blow with which his grave filled with fire. They left him until he recovered and terror left him. He said to them: For what did you strike me? They said: You prayed a prayer while you were without purification, and you passed by an oppressed man and did not aid him."
"13647","13611 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speaking on Friday while he prayed the Asr prayer with the people, sitting in the first two rakahs, when a dog passed to cut off his prayer, and he feared it would pass before him. Sad ibn Abi Waqqas supplicated against the dog, and Allah destroyed it by His power. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer and saw the dog dead, he said: Who among you supplicated against this dog? No one spoke. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated, and Sad said then: I am the one who supplicated against it, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you; I feared it would cut off your prayer, so I supplicated against it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did you supplicate against it, O Sad? Sad said: Glory be to You, there is no god but You, O Possessor of majesty and honor, destroy this dog lest it cut off the prayer of Your Prophet. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Sad, you supplicated on a day and in an hour with words that, had you supplicated against those between the heavens, it would have been answered for you. Rejoice, O Sad."
"13648","13612 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every pregnant slave girl is forbidden to her owner until she delivers what is in her womb, and every donkey worked upon, its meat is forbidden, and garlic is forbidden. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted garlic and commanded whoever eats it not to go out to the mosque until its odor is gone; it is a harm, so whoever eats it should not approach the mosque."
"13649","13613 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you dies, do not detain him, hasten with him to his grave, and let the Opening of the Book be recited at his head, and the end of al-Baqarah at his feet, in his grave."
"13650","13614 - Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no prayer for one who enters the mosque while the imam is standing praying, so he should not pray alone by himself, but should join the imam in prayer."
"13651","13615 - Abd Allah ibn Sad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Ruhawi narrated, my father related to me, from his father, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Tale-bearing, reviling, and zealous partisanship are in the Fire, and they shall not gather together in the breast of a believer."
"13652","13616 - Abd Allah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated, Maslamah ibn Ali narrated, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah performed ablution three times three times."
"13653","13617 - al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts perpetually, he has neither fasted nor broken fast."
"13654","13618 - al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."
"13655","13619 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: No people withhold the zakah of their wealth but they are withheld rain from the sky, and were it not for the cattle they would not be given rain."
"13656","13620 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, they said: Asim ibn Ali narrated, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from al-Abbas ibn Utbah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you, for there is no servant who spends the night pure but an angel spends with him in his inner garment; he does not turn in any hour of the night but it says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night pure."
"13657","13621 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated, Maymun ibn Zayd narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Sulayman ibn al-Rabi, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you. There is no servant who spends the night pure but an angel spends the night in his inner garment; whenever he turns in an hour of the night, the angel says: O Allah, forgive Your servant as he spent the night pure."
"13658","13622 - Ahmad ibn al-Jaad al-Washsha narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated, from Salim al-Aftas, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and pray behind whoever says: There is no god but Allah."
"13659","13623 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami related to me, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, from Marzuq, freedman of the family of Talhah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will never unite upon misguidance, so hold to the congregation, for the Hand of Allah is upon the congregation."
"13660","13624 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, Sulayman ibn Sufyan al-Madani narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"13661","13625 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abu al-Rabi al-Samman narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of wala, and giving it as a gift."
"13662","13626 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated, Ahmad ibn Awfa, judge of Nahr Tira, narrated, Shubah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar and Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of wala and giving it as a gift."
"13663","13627 - Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Farra narrated, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray wherever his mount turned with him."
"13664","13628 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd related to me, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon his mount."
"13665","13629 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated, Ali ibn Ubayd narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every two contracting parties, there is no sale between them until they separate, except the sale of option."
"13666","13630 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Station, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven times, and indeed there is for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"13667","13631 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, and he mentioned the same."
"13668","13632 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abi Khidash al-Mawsili narrated, Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and indeed there is for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"13669","13633 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated, he said: Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Station, and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said: {Indeed there is for you in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example}."
"13670","13634 - Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us, Adam narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar. And Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Ruzzi narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived at Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rakahs behind the Station, then went out to al-Safa from the door by which one goes out, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Ghundar added in his hadith, Shubah said: Ayyub informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that it is Sunnah."
"13671","13635 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Muadhdhin narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: As for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he arrived, circumambulated the House, then bowed two rakahs, then walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"13672","13636 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Shaatha narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed me, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, and he mentioned the same as the hadith of Ibn Jurayj."
"13673","13637 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should make his brother rise from his seat to sit in his place."
"13674","13638 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf, the two Egyptians, narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi informed me, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go to relieve himself to al-Mughammas. Nafi said: About two miles from Makkah."
"13675","13639 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the killing of dogs, except the dog of livestock or hunting."
"13676","13640 - Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever owns a slave jointly with another and frees his share, it is assessed upon him so he frees him fully."
"13677","13641 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of the Maghazi, related to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the drinker of wine and its pourer."
"13678","13642 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father related to me, Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar narrating from Jabir, Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit until its soundness appears."
"13679","13643 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Saigh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated, from Asim ibn Amr, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah when it had three hundred and eighty idols, with a staff in his hand. He pointed at them and said: {Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing}. And the idols fell down."
"13680","13644 - Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari narrated, Abu Asim narrated, from Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba and the muzaffat."
"13681","13645 - Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Tai narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obligated upon us the charity of Ramadan: a sa of barley, or a sa of dates."
"13682","13646 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Shafii al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Hashim al-Simsar narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated, Sukayn ibn Abi Siraj narrated, Amr ibn Dinar narrated, from Ibn Umar: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most beloved to Allah? And which deeds are most beloved to Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved people to Allah, exalted is He, are the most beneficial of them to people, and the most beloved deeds to Allah, exalted is He, are a joy you bring to a Muslim, or a distress you remove from him, or a debt you settle for him, or hunger you drive away from him. And for me to walk with a brother for a need is dearer to me than to seclude myself in this mosque - meaning the mosque of Madinah - for a month. Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will cover his faults, and whoever swallows his rage, though had he wished to carry it out he could have, Allah will fill his heart with hope on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever walks with his brother for a need until it is arranged for him, Allah will make his foot firm on the day feet slip."
"13683","13647 - Ubayd al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishkab narrated, Mansur ibn Suqayr narrated, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the protected area of a palm tree the reach of its fronds."
"13684","13648 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simmari narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated, Awf ibn Muhammad Abu Ghassan narrated, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulate after the dawn prayer, then pray two rakahs, then say: It is only disliked at sunrise, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan."
"13685","13649 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar, Abdan ibn Ahmad, and al-Hasan ibn Abd Allah al-Kindi al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated, Salih ibn Ziyad narrated, Amr ibn Dinar narrated, he said: I saw Ibn Umar dyeing his beard yellow. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do I see you touch none of the corners except the Yemeni corner and the Black Stone? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe none but them. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do I see you wear nothing but Sibti sandals? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wear none but them. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do I see you not chant the talbiyah until your mount stands straight with you? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that."
"13686","13650 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated, Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated, Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: While we sat in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a woman passed, and some of the people said: This is the daughter of Muhammad. A man said: The likeness of Muhammad among Banu Hashim is like sweet basil amid stench. The woman went and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with anger known in his face until he stood over the people and said: What is with statements reaching me from some people? Allah, mighty and majestic, created the heavens and the earth as seven, chose the highest of them and dwelt therein, and settled in His heavens whom He willed of His creation. He created the earth as seven and chose the highest of them and settled therein whom He willed of His creation. He created mankind and chose from mankind the children of Adam, chose from the children of Adam the Arabs, chose from the Arabs Mudar, chose from Mudar Quraysh, chose from Quraysh Banu Hashim, and chose me from Banu Hashim. So I am the choicest unto the choicest. Whoever loves the Arabs, it is for love of me he loves them, and whoever hates the Arabs, it is for hatred of me he hates them."
"13687","13651 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated, Warqa narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umrah, for they erase sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"13688","13652 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar: that Ibn Umar was asked about a man who says to a man: Sell me the fruit of your land for what you used to measure from it. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, and it is muzabanah."
"13689","13653 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated, my father narrated, Ibn Jurayj narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rakahs before Zuhr, two rakahs after Friday, two rakahs after Maghrib, and two rakahs after Isha."
"13690","13654 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated, Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated, Warqa ibn Umar narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at al-Hijr, he said: Do not enter upon these punished people. Then he ordered the dough to be thrown away."
"13691","13655 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated, Ibn Thawban related to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the coming year. When the first night of Ramadan comes, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and scatters the leaves of Paradise, and the wide-eyed houris come saying: O Lord, appoint for us husbands from Your servants in whom our eyes find delight and their eyes find delight in us."
"13692","13656 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, Yahya ibn Ziyad narrated, Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The master of days with Allah is Friday; in it Adam, your father, was created, in it he entered Paradise, in it he left it, and in it the Hour will come."
"13693","13657 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated, Zayd ibn Hibban narrated, from al-Khuzi - meaning Ibrahim ibn Yazid - from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: Ibn al-Zubayr claims that one or two sucks in nursing do not prohibit? Ibn Umar said: The decree of Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger is better than the decree of Ibn al-Zubayr; little nursing and much of it are the same."
"13694","13658 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I have not placed a brick upon a brick nor planted since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away."
"13695","13659 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated, my father narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What garments may the pilgrim in ihram wear? He said: He should not wear any garment touched by wars or saffron."
"13696","13660 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever seeks Laylat al-Qadr, let him seek it in the last seven or on the twenty-seventh."
"13697","13661 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Shadhan ibn Uthman ibn Jabalah ibn Abi Rawwad narrated, my father narrated, from my grandfather, from Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever seeks Laylat al-Qadr, it is the night of the twenty-seventh."
"13698","13662 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukarram narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Ghaylani narrated, Abu Qutaybah narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"13699","13663 - Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated, Shubah narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it."
"13700","13664 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated, Ahmad ibn Awfa, judge of Nahr Tira, related to me, Shubah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar and Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: When we pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon hearing and obeying, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prompt us: As much as you are able."
"13701","13665 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Abu Nuhayk eats much. Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine. Abu Nuhayk said: As for me, I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"13702","13666 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey upon a difficult young camel belonging to Umar ibn al-Khattab. The young camel overcame me and went ahead of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umar forbade me and shouted at me. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what I suffered from the young camel and what I suffered from Umar, he said to Umar: Will you sell the young camel? He said: Rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Rather for a price. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought it and said: It is yours, O Abd Allah; go and do with it as you wish."
"13703","13667 - Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated, Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar mentioning from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: When a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I owe the freeing of a slave from the children of Ismail, he would say: Free Hasan and Husayn."
"13704","13668 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Isa al-Dubai narrated, Abd al-Ala narrated, Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that he saw Suhayl, and Ibn Umar said: May Allah curse Suhayl. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Suhayl was a tax-collector among the tax-collectors of Yemen, so Allah transformed him and hung him where you see."
"13705","13669 - Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a handful of blood you shed stand between any of you and Paradise."
"13706","13670 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Ibn Umar, when Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman, freedman of Urwah, asked him: What do you say about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating? He said: Abd Allah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him take her back. So he returned her to me and did not count it as anything. He said: When she is pure, let him divorce or keep her. Ibn Umar said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: (O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at the beginning of their waiting period)."
"13707","13671 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the pitched jar and the gourd."
"13708","13672 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub Dallawayh related to me, al-Harith ibn al-Numan Abu al-Nadr narrated, Warqa ibn Umar narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah: that Ibn Umar entered ihram twice from Makkah, and entered ihram the third time when his mount stood straight with him. He said: I did not know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to enter ihram by it except when facing forward."
"13709","13673 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Zayd al-Dabbagh narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Sufayra narrated, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed is he who met me, believed in me, and affirmed me; blessed is he who met me, believed in me, and affirmed me; and blessed is he who did not meet me yet believed in me and affirmed me."
"13710","13674 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated, Amir ibn Mudrik narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: I asked Ibn Umar: In which month did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform Umrah? He said: In Rajab."
"13711","13675 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Ali al-Azdi, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about silk? He said: We heard that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"13712","13676 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, al-Saq ibn Hazn narrated, from Qatadah, Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Bariqi narrated, he said: A woman in Makkah asked me for a ruling. I said: This is Abd Allah ibn Umar; go to him and ask him. She hurried toward him and I followed her to hear what she said. She said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Give me a ruling about cheese. He said: What is cheese? She said to him: Something made from milk, so-and-so, and they curdle the rennet. He said: Whatever the Muslims and the People of the Book make, eat it; and whatever they do not make, do not eat it. She said: O Abd Allah, give me a ruling about locusts. He said: Its eating is lawful slaughter. She said: O Abd Allah, give me a ruling about gold. He said: It is disliked for men. She said: Then give me a ruling about silk. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"13713","13677 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah informed me, from Qatadah, from Ali al-Bariqi, from Ibn Umar, when a man asked him about wearing silk? He said: We used to say that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"13714","13678 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father related to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Bariqi: that he asked Ibn Umar about silk? He said: We used to say that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"13715","13679 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shubah narrated, from Yala ibn Ata, from Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Bariqi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prayer of night and day is two by two."
"13716","13680 - al-Sari ibn Sahl al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Rushayd narrated, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from Qatadah, from Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Bariqi, from Ibn Umar, about silk, he said: We used to say that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"13717","13681 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that Ali al-Azdi informed him that Ibn Umar informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he mounted his camel going out on a journey, would say takbir three times, then say: {Glory to Him who subjected this to us} until: {and indeed to our Lord we shall return}. O Allah, we ask You in this journey of ours righteousness and piety, and of deeds what pleases You. O Allah, lighten for us this journey of ours and fold for us its distance. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, and an evil sight in family. And when he returned he would say them and add therein: Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising."
"13718","13682 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ali ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and mounted his riding animal and it set out with him, he would say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. Then he would say: {Glory to Him who subjected this to us though we could not master it * and indeed to our Lord we shall return}. O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine righteousness and piety, and of deeds what pleases You. O Allah, lighten for us travel and fold for us its distance. O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over family. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return in family and wealth. Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising."
"13719","13683 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Arfajah, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I intend to go to al-Tur? He said: Journeys are undertaken only to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, and al-Aqsa Mosque. Leave al-Tur and do not go to it."
"13720","13684 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, and he heard Abu al-Abbas al-Ama narrating from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged al-Taif and could gain nothing from them. He said: We shall return tomorrow, Allah willing. That weighed upon the Muslims, and they said: Shall we return without conquering it?! He said: Then go forth to battle in the morning. They went forth in the morning and wounds befell them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall return tomorrow, Allah willing. They fell silent, and that pleased them, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled."
"13721","13685 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ismail al-Shaybani, he said: I sold what was on the tops of my palms for a hundred wasqs, with any increase for them and any shortfall upon them. I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, except that he permitted al-araya."
"13722","13686 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated, Musa ibn Rabiah narrated, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Dinar: that Ismail al-Shaybani related to him that he sold palms for a hundred wasqs in fulfillment from what was on the tops of his palms; if it increased it was for them, and if it decreased it was upon them. He asked Abd Allah ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this sale, except that he permitted the sale of al-araya."
"13723","13687 - al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb, he said: We went out with Ibn Umar and the sun set. We were too awed by Ibn Umar to say to him: The prayer. He waited until the whiteness of the horizon had gone and the darkness of Isha came, then alighted and prayed three rakahs. Then he led us in two rakahs, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"13724","13688 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated, Shubah narrated, Ibn Abi Najih related to me, from his father: that a man asked Ibn Umar about fasting the day of Arafah. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, nor do I forbid you nor command you; if you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"13725","13689 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated. And Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated, they said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated, Abu Bishr Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah narrated, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever sells palms that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"13726","13690 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated, Abd al-Warith narrated, from Ayyub, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one wailed over is punished."
"13727","13691 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated, Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated, from Rabah ibn Abi Maruf, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, he said: A man said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I see you touch the two corners and never leave them? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch them and never leave them. The man said: Do you not touch the other two corners? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not touch them."
"13728","13692 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yunus ibn al-Qasim Abu Umar al-Yamami, whom I met at Makkah, narrated, Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever magnifies himself in his soul and struts in his walk will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"13729","13693 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yunus ibn al-Qasim narrated, Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted while traveling and broke fast."
"13730","13694 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Ibn Umar: that a man bought land with its fruit from a man, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fruit belongs to the one who pollinated it, unless he stipulates - meaning the buyer."
"13731","13695 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated, Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated, Badr ibn Uthman narrated, from Ubayd Allah ibn Marwan, from Abu Aishah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one morning and said: Just before dawn I saw as though I was given the keys and the scales. As for the keys, these are the keys, and as for the scales, these are what you weigh with. I was placed in a pan and my ummah was placed in a pan, and I outweighed them. Then Abu Bakr was brought and placed in a pan and my ummah was placed in a pan, and he outweighed them. Then Umar was brought and placed in a pan and my ummah was placed in a pan, and he outweighed them. Then Uthman was brought and placed in a pan and my ummah was placed in a pan, and he outweighed them. Then the scales were lifted. Abu al-Qasim said: Abu Aishah in my view is Masruq ibn al-Ajda, and Allah knows best."
"13732","13696 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated, Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr ibn Mansur al-Mashriqi, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought cheese in the expedition of Tabuk. He took a knife and cut, and said: Eat in the name of Allah. Abu al-Qasim said: al-Mashriqiyyin is a clan of Hamdan."
"13733","13697 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, they said: al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated, Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, he said: A man said to Ibn Umar: We enter upon these rulers and say to them, then when we leave we say about them otherwise? He said: We used to count this hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13734","13698 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Sinan ibn Harun narrated, from Mujalid, from Amir, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, some people command us to ascend the pulpits and speak, yet when we descend, by Allah, for one of us to fall from the sky is dearer to him than to utter anything of it? He said: This was hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13735","13699 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated, Yahya ibn Ismail ibn Salim narrated, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given choice between this world and the Hereafter, and he chose the Hereafter."
"13736","13700 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi narrated, they said: Sharik narrated, from Jabir, meaning al-Jufi, from Amir al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established the travel prayer as two rakahs, and they are complete, and the witr in travel is of the Sunnah."
"13737","13701 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated, Sharik narrated, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, he said: May Allah curse whoever claims that I migrated before my father; he only sent me ahead with his baggage."
"13738","13702 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated, my father narrated, Shubah narrated, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from al-Shabi, he heard Ibn Umar saying: There were people of his Companions with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Sad. They were brought lizard meat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat, for it is lawful, but it is not of my food."
"13739","13703 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated, my father narrated, Shubah narrated, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from al-Shabi, he said: I accompanied Ibn Umar and never heard him narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except the hadith of the lizard."
"13740","13704 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated, Shubah informed me, Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar informed me, he said: I heard al-Shabi saying: I sat with Ibn Umar for a year and never heard him narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13741","13705 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrating from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir, he said: I wish I could meet this ram and forbid him his saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - I was with Ibn Umar for two years and he narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only the hadith of the lizard. Abu al-Qasim said: By his saying the ram he means al-Hasan al-Basri."
"13742","13706 - al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated, Khalid ibn Abi Khalid al-Azraq al-Sulami narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best worship is understanding, and the best religion is scrupulousness."
"13743","13707 - Abu Shuayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik al-Halabi Abu Khalid al-Zuhri, freedman of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, narrated, he said: I heard Amir al-Shabi saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays Duha, fasts three days of the month, and never leaves witr in travel or residence, the reward of a martyr will be written for him."
"13744","13708 - Abu Shuayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Bablutti narrated, Ayyub ibn Nahik narrated, he said: I heard Amir al-Shabi saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you enters the mosque while the imam is on the pulpit, there is no prayer and no speech until the imam finishes."
"13745","13709 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Khalid narrated, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, he said: We met the enemy, and the Muslims wheeled away in retreat. I was among those who wheeled away. We said: We have incurred wrath from Allah and His Messenger. Then we said: If only we entered Madinah and stocked provisions in it! So we entered Madinah and waited for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he came out to prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we are the deserters!! He said: Rather you are those who return to battle; I am a refuge for you."
"13746","13710 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated, Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, make odd with one rakah, for Allah is Odd and loves the odd."
"13747","13711 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, Salamah ibn Kuhayl and al-Hakam related to us, they said: Said ibn Jubayr led us in prayer at Jam: Maghrib three rakahs. When he gave salam, he stood and prayed Isha two rakahs. Then he narrated from Ibn Umar that he did the same in that place. Then Ibn Umar narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did the same in that place."
"13748","13712 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah al-Bajali, from Said ibn Jubayr al-Asadi: that he poured forth from Arafat. Al-Hakam said: I followed him while he was upon a camel of his, urging it no more than a trot. I said: This one accompanied Abd Allah ibn Abbas and Abd Allah ibn Umar, so I shall see how he acts? He traveled until he came to Jam. He alighted, and no sooner had we put down our saddles than he established the prayer. Then he led us in Maghrib. I hardly knew until he stood, said takbir, and prayed the night prayer. He led us, then said: Thus I saw Abd Allah ibn Umar do. Then Abd Allah ibn Umar related to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did thus."
"13749","13713 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: We poured forth with Ibn Umar until he came to Jam. He led us in Maghrib and Isha with one iqamah. Then he turned and said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer."
"13750","13714 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father related to me. And Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated, they said: Hushaym narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: Wine is cursed, and its presser, its commissioner, its drinker, and its pourer."
"13751","13715 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, he said: Ayyub said: Amr ibn Dinar related to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar: that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what of my dowry? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you are truthful, it is hers for what you made lawful of her; and if you are lying, it is more binding upon him - or as he said regarding the two who invoke curses."
"13752","13716 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar: that he passed by people who had taken a hen as a target, shooting at it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever mutilates animals."
"13753","13717 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, al-Amash narrated, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking animals as targets."
"13754","13718 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shubah narrated, al-Minhal ibn Amr informed me, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr saying: I went out with Ibn Umar on a road of Madinah, and he saw boys shooting at a hen. Ibn Umar said: Who did this?! They scattered. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever makes an example of a living creature."
"13755","13719 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking a living soul as a target."
"13756","13720 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ubayd narrated, Hushaym narrated, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade killing any beast by confinement."
"13757","13721 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Fudayl ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Umar passed by people who had set up a hen, shooting at it with arrows. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever mutilates animals."
"13758","13722 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah related to me, from al-Nadr ibn Muhammad, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from al-Fudayl ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursing whoever mutilates animals."
"13759","13723 - Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, Abu Hariz related to me that he heard Said ibn Jubayr saying: A man asked Abd Allah ibn Umar about fasting the day of Arafah? He said: We used to equate it, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with fasting a year."
"13760","13724 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Wadih al-Assal narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated, Muhammad ibn Jafar informed me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, while I listened, about Laylat al-Qadr? He said: It is in every Ramadan."
"13761","13725 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Said narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, Said ibn Jubayr narrated, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray upon his mount while coming from Makkah to Madinah wherever it turned with him, and concerning him this verse was sent down: {So wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah}."
"13762","13726 - Abu Man Thabit ibn Nuaym al-Huji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars, taking this for this and this for this, giving this for this and this for this. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Hafsah, and said: O Messenger of Allah, wait a moment while I ask you: I sell camels at al-Baqi, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, selling for dirhams and taking dinars, taking this for this and giving this for this? He said: There is no harm in taking them at the rate of the day, so long as you do not separate while something remains between you."
"13763","13727 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated, Israil informed me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I used to sell at al-Baqi for dirhams and take dinars, taking dirhams for dinars and dinars for dirhams. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: When you take one of them for the other, your companion must not leave you while a sale remains between you."
"13764","13728 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Isa ibn Ali al-Askari narrated, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Bahram al-Hiti narrated, my father narrated, from Mansur, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Relate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah will bring the believing servant on the Day of Resurrection until He places him in His veil. He will say to him: Read in your record. He will read, and He will make him acknowledge sin by sin, saying to him: Do you recognize? Do you recognize? He will say: Yes, my Lord. He will say: Read. He will read and glance right and left. He will say: There is no harm upon you, My servant; you are in My cover; none but Me looks upon your sins. Go, for I have forgiven them for you. It will be said to him: Enter Paradise. As for the disbeliever, it will be said over the heads of witnesses: {These are those who lied against their Lord; indeed the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers}."
"13765","13729 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) anointed himself while in ihram with unscented oil."
"13766","13730 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about the nabidh of the jar? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"13767","13731 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of the jar."
"13768","13732 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated, Hammam informed me, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of the jar."
"13769","13733 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated, Muan ibn Rifaaah narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi Amrah related to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever mutilates an animal, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"13770","13734 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, I think he raised it, he said: The woman in her pregnancy until delivery until weaning is like one stationed in the path of Allah; if she dies in between, she has the reward of a martyr."
"13771","13735 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated, from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: This verse was sent down upon us: {Then indeed you on the Day of Resurrection before your Lord will dispute}. We did not know its explanation until tribulation occurred, and we said: This is what we were promised - woe to us! - that we would dispute about it."
"13772","13736 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Shaqiq Abu Wail: that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back, then divorce her when she is pure."
"13773","13737 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father related to me, he said: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting, Mustalim ibn Said narrated, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Abu Wail: that a man said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: You perform Hajj but do not raid! He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House."
"13774","13738 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh related to me, Abu Awanah narrated, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a stray date, took it, and handed it to a beggar. He said: Had you not come to it, it would have come to you."
"13775","13739 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated, Ismail ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated, from Bashir ibn Salman, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: We were with Ibn Umar while a boy of his skinned a sheep. He said to him: Woe to you! When you finish, begin with our Jewish neighbor. It was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how often you mention this Jew! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoining the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"13776","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from 'Uthman Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadham, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three shall be upon dunes of musk: a man who led a people in prayer while they are pleased with him, a man who calls to the five prayers by day and night, and a slave who fulfilled the right of Allah and the right of his masters."
"13777","Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadham, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is prompted with ""there is no god but Allah"" at his death shall enter Paradise."
"13778","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abu Dihaqanah, from Ibn 'Umar: Bilal exchanged two sa's (of dates for one), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it, return it."
"13779","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Firas, from Abu Salih, from Zadham: Ibn 'Umar freed a slave of his, then took a stick from the ground and said: I have no reward in it worth even this; then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever slaps his slave or beats him for a prescribed penalty he did not incur, its expiation is to free him."
"13780","Ishaq narrated, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Firas, a similar report."
"13781","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah reported, from Zayd ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar about touching the (Black) Stone? He said: We used to tap it with a stick."
"13782","'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Isra'il reported, from Zayd ibn Jubayr who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar when a man asked him: I am ill and cannot touch the Stone? He said: When we were in such a state we would tap it with a stick and touch it thereby."
"13783","Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih al-'Ijli narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr: A man mentioned to Ibn 'Umar the Stone and wiping it, being prevented from it so he cannot wipe it? So Abdullah said: We used to tap it with a stick when we could not wipe it."
"13784","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for the people of Madinah (the miqat) at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Syria at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd at Qarn."
"13785","Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, Zayd ibn Jubayr narrated to me, saying: I asked Ibn 'Umar: From where is it permissible for me to enter 'umrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for the people of Madinah (the miqat) at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Syria at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd at Qarn."
"13786","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar: From where should I perform 'umrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for the people of Madinah (the miqat) at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Syria at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd at Qarn."
"13787","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying fruit until its ripeness appears."
"13788","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears."
"13789","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears."
"13790","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram may kill the kite, the crow, the vicious dog, the mouse, and the scorpion."
"13791","'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Isra'il reported, from Adam ibn 'Ali who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar about drinks, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade (nabidh in) the gourd, the hantam, the muzaffat, and the naqir."
"13792","'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Isra'il reported, from Adam ibn 'Ali who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: All nations shall come on the Day of Resurrection kneeling, each nation with its prophet; then the prophet comes with his nation and they are raised with them upon a mound above the nations, and they say: O so-and-so, intercede; O so-and-so, intercede. They refer one to another until they reach the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and that is the saying of Allah, the Almighty: ""Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station."""
"13793","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated, my father and my uncle narrated, from their father, from Ibn Ishaq, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to me, from Adam ibn 'Ali, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spread your forearms as the beast spreads, support yourself upon your palms, and keep your elbows away from your sides."
"13794","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simmari narrated to us, both saying: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn 'Uthman narrated, Abu Dawud narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Adam ibn 'Ali, who heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fruit is not to be sold until it ripens."
"13795","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Fasawi al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated, Abu Shaybah al-Qadi narrated, from Adam ibn 'Ali, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No people ever perished except at the time of the adhan, and the Hour shall not come except at the time of the adhan. Abu al-Qasim said: In my view, and Allah knows best, its meaning is the time of the Fajr adhan, which is the time of seeking forgiveness and supplication."
"13796","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-'Ala ibn 'Arar who said: Ibn 'Umar was asked about 'Ali and 'Uthman, and he said: As for 'Ali, do not ask about him; look at his position with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he closed our doors in the mosque and left his door open. As for 'Uthman, he committed a great sin on the day the two hosts met, and Allah pardoned him, then he committed against you a lesser sin and you killed him."
"13797","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Zadham who said: I said to Ibn 'Umar: Tell me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade of vessels? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hantamah, which is the jar, forbade the gourd, forbade the naqir, which is the palm trunk hollowed and carved out, forbade the muzaffat, which is the pitched vessel, and commanded drinking from skins."
"13798","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Abu 'Awanah narrated, from Firas, from Abu Salih, from Zadham Abu 'Umar: Ibn 'Umar freed a boy of his, then took a stick from the ground and said: I have no reward in it worth even this; then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever slaps his slave or beats him for a prescribed penalty he did not incur, its expiation is to free him."
"13799","Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, Sharik reported, from Firas, from Abu Salih, from Zadham who said: I was sitting with Ibn 'Umar when a boy of his passed by, and he said: You are free — or he said: You belong to Allah — then he lifted a stick from the ground and said: I have no reward in it equal to this. I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman?! He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wrongs his slave or flogs him for a prescribed penalty he did not incur, its expiation is to free him."
"13800","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, Ibn 'A'ishah narrated, Safwan ibn 'Isa narrated, Isma'il ibn Muslim narrated, saying: I was with al-A'mash when flies kept falling on his eyes; he kept waving them off and they returned, so he said: O Isma'il, what do you remember about flies? He said: I remember that the lifespan of a fly is forty days; as if I did not satisfy him about them. He said: Khaythamah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn 'Umar — or he said: Ibn 'Amr — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee."
